WEBVTT

00:06.215 --> 00:07.299
[theme song playing]

00:07.382 --> 00:10.469
[in English]
♪ You're driving alone at night ♪

00:10.969 --> 00:14.723
♪ You're driving alone at night ♪

00:15.474 --> 00:20.479
♪ Deep in the silence
But it doesn't mean you're lost ♪

00:20.562 --> 00:23.690
♪ And I'll tell you what ♪

00:24.358 --> 00:27.236
♪ We're on the train ♪

00:27.319 --> 00:31.198
♪ I promise I'll be where you are ♪

00:31.740 --> 00:35.953
♪ If any thought is against you ♪

00:36.036 --> 00:39.581
♪ With you, I am starting over ♪

00:39.665 --> 00:43.710
♪ We're learning to walk again ♪

00:43.794 --> 00:45.462
OUR UNWRITTEN SEOUL

00:45.546 --> 00:46.588
[song concludes]

00:46.672 --> 00:49.383
[in Korean] Gosh,
the Hangang River is amazing.

00:49.466 --> 00:52.302
Aren't you hungry?
Want to get some ramyun?

00:52.386 --> 00:54.388
Wait, what time's the fountain show?

00:54.471 --> 00:55.806
Should we eat after watching it?

00:55.889 --> 00:57.766
No, maybe we should wait until sunset…

00:57.849 --> 00:58.934
Mi-ji.

01:00.060 --> 01:03.730
[soft dreamy music playing]

01:10.654 --> 01:11.989
You're Mi-ji, aren't you?

01:21.415 --> 01:22.374
No, I'm not.

01:25.544 --> 01:26.420
You're not?

01:26.503 --> 01:27.504
[scoffs]

01:28.505 --> 01:31.466
You think I'm Mi-ji?
What makes you say that?

01:31.550 --> 01:33.510
Why do you think I'm her?

01:33.594 --> 01:37.848
The way you were talking
and acting was just like Mi-ji.

01:38.515 --> 01:40.183
You seemed just like her.

01:40.267 --> 01:41.810
-I see.
-[music fades]

01:41.893 --> 01:43.478
So you're saying

01:43.562 --> 01:46.356
I'm not allowed to be cheerful
when I'm happy or excited?

01:46.440 --> 01:49.526
-No, that's not what I meant--
-[Mi-ji] That's exactly what you meant.

01:49.610 --> 01:51.945
Mi-ji is allowed to get excited,
but I'm not?

01:52.029 --> 01:53.697
No, I'm just saying

01:54.531 --> 01:56.825
that you seem a bit different
from your usual self--

01:56.908 --> 01:58.327
My "usual self"?

01:58.410 --> 01:59.411
[scoffs]

01:59.494 --> 02:01.288
Do you even know me that well?

02:01.913 --> 02:05.083
We've hardly seen each other.
How dare you act like you know me!

02:08.003 --> 02:09.838
I'm sorry if I upset you.

02:09.921 --> 02:11.715
I didn't mean anything bad.

02:11.798 --> 02:14.426
This is why I said you're self-absorbed.

02:14.509 --> 02:17.888
You always act like you know everything,
as if you have all the answers.

02:17.971 --> 02:20.223
Why can't you think of Mi-ji and me
as two separate people?

02:20.307 --> 02:23.310
How could you ask me if I'm Mi-ji?

02:23.393 --> 02:25.145
Did you really mean that?

02:26.521 --> 02:29.149
[soft pensive music playing]

02:32.110 --> 02:34.655
No, I was joking.

02:40.202 --> 02:41.536
[Mi-ji] It closed.

02:43.372 --> 02:45.207
Don't make jokes like that anymore.

02:46.124 --> 02:48.543
If you have nothing else to say,
let's get going.

02:59.262 --> 03:01.264
[Mi-ji]
A person's heart is like a door.

03:01.348 --> 03:02.683
RAINBOW FOUNTAIN SHUT DOWN

03:02.766 --> 03:05.894
And I'm an expert at knowing
exactly when that door is closing.

03:06.436 --> 03:09.690
-Mom! Look at me!
-[soft pensive music continues]

03:11.817 --> 03:13.276
Mom!

03:13.360 --> 03:15.195
Come down. It's dangerous.
You're going to fall.

03:15.278 --> 03:17.614
-Mom, come on. Look at me.
-[Ok-hui] Yes, she's very active.

03:17.698 --> 03:19.074
-Mom!
-[Mi-ji] Since I was young,

03:19.157 --> 03:21.827
I had a hard time getting people
to open their hearts to me.

03:21.910 --> 03:22.953
[young Mi-ji] Mom!

03:23.036 --> 03:26.081
[Ok-hui] Here they come. Mi-rae!

03:26.623 --> 03:28.125
Your sister's coming. Come on!

03:28.625 --> 03:29.668
Mi-rae!

03:29.751 --> 03:31.586
[tepidly] Mom!

03:32.337 --> 03:34.756
[Mi-ji] I even struggled with my mom…

03:34.840 --> 03:36.883
-Eat this on the way.
-…who was supposed to be easy.

03:36.967 --> 03:38.510
Please look at me.

03:41.430 --> 03:42.764
[gate closes]

03:43.390 --> 03:45.559
[Mi-ji] And then I met Ho-su.

03:46.309 --> 03:49.229
[tender music playing]

03:49.312 --> 03:52.065
[chalk tapping on blackboard]

04:02.451 --> 04:03.994
-[Mi-ji whispering]
-Oh?

04:06.913 --> 04:08.165
[loudly] Why--

04:08.874 --> 04:10.375
[teacher] What? What's wrong?

04:12.210 --> 04:13.128
[music fades]

04:13.211 --> 04:15.130
I understand why it's like that.

04:15.213 --> 04:16.965
-What do you mean?
-[chuckles]

04:17.048 --> 04:19.092
Why the graph goes like this.

04:20.385 --> 04:22.512
This? You already get it?

04:22.596 --> 04:24.139
Do the rest of you get it too?

04:24.222 --> 04:26.933
-[class] No, sir.
-[student] We don't.

04:27.017 --> 04:28.143
[overlapping chatter]

04:28.226 --> 04:31.521
[teacher] Ho-su is a bit fast.
You guys are normal.

04:31.605 --> 04:32.731
[soft pop song playing]

04:32.814 --> 04:36.151
[singing in Korean]

04:36.234 --> 04:38.653
[Mi-ji]
A laugh shared by just the two of us.

04:38.737 --> 04:40.155
[sobs]

04:41.448 --> 04:42.449
Hey.

04:42.949 --> 04:44.618
[Mi-ji] And tears shed in secret.

04:44.701 --> 04:46.745
[Ho-su continues sobbing]

04:46.828 --> 04:50.457
[singing in Korean continues]

04:50.540 --> 04:55.378
[Mi-ji] Ho-su's heart seemed like a door
that would never crack open.

05:02.886 --> 05:03.887
[gate opens]

05:03.970 --> 05:07.849
[Mi-ji] And when I caught a glimpse of him
through that crack, my heart raced…

05:08.850 --> 05:10.644
[singing in Korean continues]

05:10.727 --> 05:12.020
…like it did when I was running.

05:12.103 --> 05:14.564
-I'm so full.
-Me too.

05:16.983 --> 05:19.694
-Hey, it's Ho-su.
-[friend] What?

05:19.778 --> 05:20.946
Hey, Ho-su…

05:21.029 --> 05:23.949
The joy of knowing that even I had
a door I could open was short-lived.

05:24.032 --> 05:25.867
I heard Mi-rae and Ho-su are dating.

05:26.368 --> 05:27.285
What?

05:27.911 --> 05:29.371
Who told you that?

05:29.454 --> 05:30.705
Everyone's saying it.

05:31.373 --> 05:33.291
They're the top two students
in the school,

05:33.375 --> 05:35.043
so the teachers are letting it slide.

05:35.126 --> 05:36.294
[Mi-ji scoffs]

05:36.378 --> 05:38.547
There's no way Mi-rae would date Ho-su.

05:39.297 --> 05:40.757
[Mi-ji] I grew anxious.

05:41.466 --> 05:45.804
I was worried that someone else might open
the only door that I was able to open.

05:46.513 --> 05:48.139
[student] Hey, Mi-ji!

05:48.223 --> 05:50.725
Take it easy and don't scare the others.

05:50.809 --> 05:52.310
-Where's Ho-su?
-Ho-su?

05:53.186 --> 05:56.022
He said he was coming with Mi-rae,
but they're still not here.

05:56.106 --> 05:57.315
[song concludes]

05:57.399 --> 05:58.483
I can do it!

05:59.359 --> 06:00.443
[crowd cheering]

06:00.527 --> 06:03.613
-Go!
-Run!

06:03.697 --> 06:07.993
[students chanting] Go, Mi-ji!

06:08.076 --> 06:09.744
[student] Go! One, two! Yes!

06:09.828 --> 06:11.371
[cheering fades]

06:11.538 --> 06:13.832
[melancholic music playing]

06:14.082 --> 06:18.920
[Mi-ji] But even that door slammed shut
right before my eyes.

06:21.256 --> 06:22.173
[groans]

06:22.257 --> 06:24.342
[crowd chattering]

06:31.224 --> 06:32.309
[groans]

06:32.392 --> 06:34.311
[panting]

06:34.394 --> 06:37.564
[whimpering]

06:37.647 --> 06:39.399
[Mi-ji] That's how I became an expert.

06:39.482 --> 06:40.358
[groans]

06:40.442 --> 06:41.902
I'm all too familiar…

06:41.985 --> 06:44.321
-My leg. It hurts.
-…with the moment a door shuts before me.

06:44.404 --> 06:46.907
[sobbing]

06:46.990 --> 06:48.199
It hurts.

06:50.952 --> 06:52.370
[music concludes]

06:52.454 --> 06:56.249
EPISODE 3
KNOCK, KNOCK! PLEASE OPEN YOUR HEART

07:00.837 --> 07:02.005
Ah…

07:02.088 --> 07:03.298
Hello.

07:08.595 --> 07:10.472
Did you read the proposal inside the--

07:10.555 --> 07:11.932
[Ro-sa] I decline.

07:13.058 --> 07:15.977
Pardon? But when you called me yesterday…

07:16.061 --> 07:18.021
I said I'd treat you with respect

07:18.104 --> 07:20.899
since we're both just trying
to make a living.

07:20.982 --> 07:23.109
-Uh…
-[dramatic quirky music playing]

07:23.193 --> 07:24.110
Oh.

07:24.235 --> 07:25.320
All right.

07:26.029 --> 07:28.406
I respectfully decline the offer.

07:28.990 --> 07:31.785
I have no intention
of selling the building.

07:33.536 --> 07:35.288
But why…

07:35.372 --> 07:36.373
I…

07:39.584 --> 07:41.086
-[Gyeong-min] So…
-[sighs]

07:41.169 --> 07:43.296
-…she refused your offer?
-[music concludes]

07:43.380 --> 07:45.715
If you were just going to ask
the landowner for her opinion,

07:45.799 --> 07:47.717
then you should've just texted her.

07:47.801 --> 07:49.636
You should've just created a poll

07:49.719 --> 07:52.764
so she could vote
on whether to sell it or not.

07:52.847 --> 07:55.684
She doesn't have a smartphone.

07:55.767 --> 07:57.811
-[Gyeong-min sighs]
-[quirky music playing]

07:57.894 --> 07:58.895
Well…

07:58.979 --> 08:02.440
I don't care if she uses
a walkie-talkie or a phone.

08:02.524 --> 08:05.402
I didn't tell you to find out
what she was thinking.

08:05.485 --> 08:08.697
If she doesn't want to sell,
then convince her to. That's your job.

08:08.780 --> 08:11.574
Whether you use words or actions,

08:12.409 --> 08:14.661
persuade her
with that brilliant brain of yours.

08:14.744 --> 08:17.414
What am I supposed to do
when she doesn't want to sell?

08:17.497 --> 08:19.749
You're the pro. Why are you asking me?

08:20.667 --> 08:22.794
Aren't you an expert at luring people?

08:22.877 --> 08:24.212
[employees snickering]

08:24.295 --> 08:26.339
-What? Me?
-[music concludes]

08:26.423 --> 08:27.882
[employee coughs, clears throat]

08:27.966 --> 08:31.386
Just do what you always do.

08:32.053 --> 08:34.305
Try working your charm
on that landowner too.

08:38.435 --> 08:39.978
Who did you say he's bringing?

08:40.061 --> 08:44.158
Mr. Kim, Chairman Choi's victim,
is bringing his lawyer today.

08:44.607 --> 08:46.735
Why did he hire a lawyer
when he's coming to settle?

08:46.818 --> 08:48.862
I don't think he will be settling.

08:48.945 --> 08:52.115
He said he'll be reviewing
the entire settlement proposal again.

08:52.824 --> 08:53.742
SETTLEMENT

08:54.367 --> 08:55.869
THE VICTIM, KIM SEUNG-YONG

08:59.039 --> 09:01.082
-Why, this little…
-Pardon?

09:02.417 --> 09:05.336
Which cases is Mr. Lee handling right now?

09:05.420 --> 09:07.255
[Ye-rin] It states
that in any of those cases,

09:07.338 --> 09:09.966
Party A shall bear the burden
of paying for the test.

09:10.467 --> 09:13.178
But there's an unfair clause
in the standard business agreement

09:13.261 --> 09:16.181
that YH Group has signed
with its partner companies.

09:16.264 --> 09:17.932
It's Article 5, Paragraph 4.

09:18.016 --> 09:19.893
-But Paragraph 3--
-[Ho-su] Excuse me…

09:22.270 --> 09:23.396
I'm sorry.

09:24.147 --> 09:27.108
Was there a meeting today?
I didn't hear anything about it.

09:27.192 --> 09:28.359
Ho-su.

09:28.443 --> 09:31.529
Would you mind leaving if it's not urgent?
We're in a meeting.

09:32.072 --> 09:33.073
Continue.

09:33.740 --> 09:34.783
Yes, sir.

09:36.117 --> 09:38.870
But if the quality inspection
and component analysis conducted

09:38.953 --> 09:42.248
under Paragraph 3 reveal that
the supplied products fail to meet legal…

09:42.332 --> 09:43.374
[quirky music playing]

09:43.458 --> 09:47.337
[Se-jin] Ma'am,
I reviewed your business proposal.

09:47.420 --> 09:50.090
Thank you for specifically writing
the seedling section in bold text.

09:50.173 --> 09:52.133
I feel like it was seared into my eyes.

09:52.801 --> 09:56.137
Fine, let's work together.
We'll go look at seedlings first.

09:57.680 --> 09:58.765
Hey!

09:59.724 --> 10:02.185
Why are you getting your boots
when you're going to the hospital?

10:02.268 --> 10:04.145
I told you. I'm working at the farm again.

10:04.229 --> 10:05.271
What?

10:05.814 --> 10:08.525
Then who's going to go see Grandma?
I need to go to work.

10:08.608 --> 10:10.401
I need to go to work too.

10:10.485 --> 10:11.528
I told you yesterday.

10:11.611 --> 10:13.571
Tell them you can't go!

10:13.655 --> 10:16.157
There are plenty of other people
who can work on that farm!

10:16.241 --> 10:18.368
The caregiver is coming next week,
so until then, you--

10:18.451 --> 10:20.703
I can't do that
when I already promised to go.

10:20.787 --> 10:22.330
You tell your boss you can't work today.

10:22.413 --> 10:24.999
Hey, my work is not like yours!

10:25.083 --> 10:27.460
Why not? They're both jobs.

10:27.544 --> 10:29.045
[quirky music playing]

10:29.129 --> 10:32.340
What I mean is that you're the one
who always goes to Grandma.

10:32.423 --> 10:35.552
-So I assumed that you'd go--
-You just assumed that.

10:35.635 --> 10:37.053
But I told you that I can't.

10:37.137 --> 10:39.848
From now on, tell me ahead of time.
Don't assume things on your own.

10:39.931 --> 10:42.100
You go to the hospital today.
I'll go tomorrow.

10:44.144 --> 10:45.228
My gosh.

10:46.312 --> 10:48.523
Did she practice that last night?

10:48.606 --> 10:50.608
The words just flowed out of her mouth.

10:50.692 --> 10:51.651
Jeez.

10:53.653 --> 10:55.238
[vehicle approaching]

10:56.739 --> 10:57.699
[brakes squeal]

10:58.283 --> 11:00.034
-[engine rumbling]
-[music concludes]

11:05.790 --> 11:06.749
Get in.

11:09.335 --> 11:10.503
[Mi-rae] What is it?

11:10.587 --> 11:13.089
You told me to get in
because you had something to show me.

11:14.883 --> 11:18.803
Gosh, you're so impatient.

11:23.892 --> 11:24.767
[in English] Okay.

11:24.893 --> 11:27.020
[upbeat funky music playing]

11:27.103 --> 11:29.230
[Mi-rae yelps, breathes heavily]

11:29.314 --> 11:30.565
[sighs heavily]

11:31.983 --> 11:33.443
[Gyeong-gu hesitates]

11:33.526 --> 11:34.736
[in Korean] Well…

11:36.613 --> 11:37.697
The thing is…

11:38.281 --> 11:39.365
I…

11:40.325 --> 11:42.076
I just couldn't wait any longer.

11:43.536 --> 11:45.038
[mouths] Take a look, okay?

11:45.121 --> 11:47.332
[gasps] Oh my gosh! You're crazy!

11:47.415 --> 11:50.210
What are you doing?
Have you lost your mind?

11:50.335 --> 11:51.377
No, wait.

11:51.461 --> 11:52.545
Stop! Don't do it!

11:52.629 --> 11:54.005
-What…
-No, Mi-ji. Wait.

11:54.088 --> 11:55.256
I told you to stop!

11:55.340 --> 11:57.467
Wait! Hold on!

11:57.550 --> 11:59.802
-Give me a second. Take a look.
-I told you to stop!

11:59.886 --> 12:01.012
I said, stop! Hey!

12:01.095 --> 12:02.305
-Jeez!
-[Gyeong-gu] Hey.

12:02.388 --> 12:03.681
-[Mi-rae gasps]
-[music concludes]

12:03.765 --> 12:05.975
Come on, just look!
You told me to just do it.

12:06.059 --> 12:07.060
[Mi-rae] What?

12:07.769 --> 12:09.896
[panting]

12:14.817 --> 12:17.278
What is up with that rat?

12:17.904 --> 12:19.572
"That rat"?

12:19.656 --> 12:22.951
My Ham-cheol would feel hurt
hearing you say that.

12:23.034 --> 12:24.452
[quirky music playing]

12:24.535 --> 12:26.162
Ham-cheol.

12:27.413 --> 12:29.082
How is he doing?

12:30.959 --> 12:33.086
What are you talking about?

12:33.169 --> 12:36.089
You know Ham-cheol crossed
the rainbow bridge last year.

12:36.172 --> 12:38.258
This is a memorial tattoo, remember?

12:39.592 --> 12:41.094
Of course, he's fine.

12:41.636 --> 12:44.681
I was just saying
that he's happy in heaven.

12:44.764 --> 12:46.975
Was that so hard to understand?

12:47.475 --> 12:48.977
Hey, put your sweater back on.

12:50.228 --> 12:51.729
I misunderstood you?

12:52.438 --> 12:54.774
Come on. Just take a look.
Just one time, please?

12:54.857 --> 12:58.069
-Okay, put your sweater back on.
-Look at this. I can make it fat.

12:58.152 --> 12:59.696
It's plump Ham-cheol.

12:59.779 --> 13:02.115
-Tell me if it looks pretty.
-Yes, it does.

13:02.198 --> 13:03.825
It's plump Ham-cheol. He's…

13:10.206 --> 13:11.541
Thanks for the ride.

13:11.624 --> 13:13.751
Hey, Mi-ji.

13:15.128 --> 13:16.629
What time should I pick you up later?

13:16.713 --> 13:17.839
[sighs]

13:20.466 --> 13:22.885
You're coming to pick me up?
All the way here?

13:22.969 --> 13:25.305
You're the one who thinks of me
as your personal chauffeur.

13:25.388 --> 13:26.472
"All the way here"?

13:26.597 --> 13:29.017
I'll give you the full package today.

13:29.100 --> 13:30.935
In exchange, massage my back tonight.
My back…

13:31.019 --> 13:33.521
I think I sprained it
while moving the water bottles.

13:33.604 --> 13:36.024
I'll just go home on my own.

13:36.107 --> 13:38.034
On your own?

13:38.134 --> 13:41.237
You don't even have a bike.
You're going to walk? Let me pick you up.

13:41.321 --> 13:44.449
Don't end up running away from a boar
in the mountains like last time.

13:44.574 --> 13:46.409
I told you that it's fine.

13:46.492 --> 13:48.578
Just let me give you a ride.

13:48.661 --> 13:50.705
Why are you playing so hard to get?

13:50.788 --> 13:52.081
[Se-jin] That's enough.

13:52.165 --> 13:53.499
GYEONG-GU MART
QUICK DELIVERY

13:53.583 --> 13:57.086
Why do you think her refusal
is a sign of playing hard to get?

13:57.170 --> 13:58.129
She said it's fine.

13:59.005 --> 14:01.132
[tense quirky music playing]

14:01.966 --> 14:04.010
Why are you butting in?

14:04.135 --> 14:06.137
This is my friend…

14:06.220 --> 14:08.097
[Gyeong-gu] Wait. Hold on.

14:11.601 --> 14:14.896
You must not be from around here.

14:14.979 --> 14:19.275
Anyone living in Duson-ri
knows about our relationship.

14:20.401 --> 14:21.569
I'm her ex-boyfriend.

14:25.365 --> 14:28.368
So what?
Then you're practically a stranger.

14:28.493 --> 14:30.953
Actually, doesn't it mean
you're more dangerous than a stranger?

14:31.037 --> 14:32.705
I get why you would think that, but…

14:32.789 --> 14:34.665
[chuckles]
Hey, am I dangerous?

14:34.749 --> 14:36.959
I'll take you home
when we're done with work.

14:38.336 --> 14:39.420
You're done here now, right?

14:40.254 --> 14:41.756
Seriously, who are you?

14:41.839 --> 14:44.008
I'm Mi-ju's business partner.

14:46.135 --> 14:47.345
Gosh, it's cold.

14:48.971 --> 14:52.183
I told you that it's Mi-ji. Yu Mi-ji.

14:52.767 --> 14:55.812
Hey, Mi-ji… That guy seems weird.

14:57.939 --> 14:58.981
[music concludes]

14:59.065 --> 15:00.400
[Il-lam] So,

15:00.483 --> 15:03.903
what brings you all the way here
when you're just farming as a hobby?

15:03.986 --> 15:06.739
Somebody put this phrase
in bold and even underlined it.

15:07.323 --> 15:10.868
"In strawberry farming, choosing
the right seedling is half the battle."

15:10.952 --> 15:11.953
[Se-jin inhales]

15:12.036 --> 15:15.790
I feel like last year's harvest was a flop
because I planted whatever seedlings

15:15.873 --> 15:17.250
were given to me.

15:17.333 --> 15:19.544
What? [laughs]

15:19.627 --> 15:22.713
Now you're blaming me out of all people?

15:22.797 --> 15:24.424
Fine. Go ahead.

15:24.507 --> 15:28.803
I brought all the new varieties
you mentioned. They're all here.

15:28.886 --> 15:31.472
You two can look around
and choose the ones you want.

15:31.556 --> 15:33.766
Let's just see how good
your harvest turns out this year.

15:33.850 --> 15:34.725
Sure.

15:34.809 --> 15:36.644
[laughs]

15:41.607 --> 15:43.109
Ooh.

15:44.444 --> 15:47.905
That's the kind you need to weed out.
Even at a glance, it looks weak.

15:51.826 --> 15:54.287
The runner is thin,
and the crown is narrow.

15:54.370 --> 15:57.582
Most importantly,
there aren't enough roots.

15:58.833 --> 15:59.834
[clears throat]

16:02.628 --> 16:06.007
My harvest failed last year because
you gave me stuff like this. Am I right?

16:06.090 --> 16:08.092
-[laughs] Whatever you say.
-Jeez.

16:08.176 --> 16:09.802
-[mud squelches]
-[Se-jin grunts]

16:10.553 --> 16:11.721
My gosh…

16:20.563 --> 16:23.065
[Mi-ji] You win every battle
if you know yourself and your enemy.

16:23.149 --> 16:24.650
NO FAMILY OR FRIENDS

16:24.734 --> 16:28.529
[grumbles] I'm losing every battle
because I don't know anything about her.

16:29.489 --> 16:33.743
She only goes to her house
or the restaurant.

16:33.826 --> 16:35.620
So I can't learn anything about…

16:36.287 --> 16:37.371
Hm?

16:39.916 --> 16:40.917
[door bell chimes]

16:41.417 --> 16:42.627
[Mi-ji] She's leaving?

16:44.170 --> 16:47.757
I don't think I've ever seen her
close the restaurant at this hour.

16:47.840 --> 16:49.842
Where is she going?

16:49.926 --> 16:51.677
[gasps] She's leaving.

16:52.428 --> 16:54.931
-Oh, no!
-[suspenseful quirky music playing]

16:55.014 --> 16:56.516
[gasping]

17:04.482 --> 17:06.567
NO TO FORCED EVICTIONS
WITHOUT PROPER MEASURES

17:06.651 --> 17:08.819
POETRY READING WEDNESDAY
EVERY WEDNESDAY AT 4 PM

17:08.903 --> 17:11.280
AESIM-DONG REDEVELOPMENT
PROMOTION COMMITTEE MEETING

17:17.203 --> 17:19.914
NOVEMBER 13, 2024, WED, 4 PM
AESIM-DONG CULTURAL CENTER

17:21.707 --> 17:22.792
[sighs]

17:23.417 --> 17:25.836
[suspenseful quirky music continues]

17:26.629 --> 17:33.594
THIS WAY TO POETRY READING

17:33.678 --> 17:35.846
It feels like yesterday

17:35.972 --> 17:40.643
when the cool night air hinted
that fall was just around the corner.

17:40.726 --> 17:44.272
But there's already
a scent of winter in the wind.

17:44.855 --> 17:46.816
-When it's cold like this…
-You can have a seat.

17:46.899 --> 17:48.609
It's okay. I'm not part of the class.

17:48.693 --> 17:51.612
It's okay if you didn't register.
You're welcome to listen.

17:51.696 --> 17:54.282
-No, I should get going…
-Come on, join us.

17:54.365 --> 17:56.659
-Okay, then.
-"What Makes a Person…"

17:56.742 --> 17:58.327
You've all heard of that poem, right?

17:58.411 --> 18:01.664
We'll begin with "The Sea of Sang-wol."

18:01.747 --> 18:04.166
It's a poem that portrays
the loneliness of this season.

18:04.250 --> 18:08.212
I'll recite the poem,
and we'll discuss it afterwards.

18:09.672 --> 18:11.215
"The Sea of Sang-wol."

18:13.009 --> 18:16.804
Where did those captivated
By the sparkle go?

18:18.139 --> 18:20.725
Summer fireworks that spat out
Flashes of light

18:21.434 --> 18:23.894
All cooled down in the sand
Before we realized it

18:23.978 --> 18:25.563
"THE SEA OF SANG-WOL"

18:25.646 --> 18:28.482
-Where did all those people go?
-[indistinct chatter]

18:28.566 --> 18:31.569
[pensive music playing]

18:34.780 --> 18:37.825
[Mi-ji reciting]
Where did all those people go?

18:39.118 --> 18:40.244
[whistle blows]

18:41.871 --> 18:45.499
[Mi-ji] A stretch of cold sand where
Even the footprints have disappeared

18:46.459 --> 18:49.837
With nowhere to go, I stand by myself

18:57.386 --> 18:59.263
Like a child who lost a shoe

19:00.806 --> 19:02.391
I wander all by myself

19:04.644 --> 19:06.270
Now barefoot

19:08.022 --> 19:09.857
I have nowhere else to return to

19:09.940 --> 19:13.277
ADMISSION TO THE DEPARTMENT
OF PHYSICAL EDUCATION AS TOP OF THE CLASS

19:13.819 --> 19:15.905
When I hold the conch to my ear

19:15.988 --> 19:20.701
I can still vividly hear the fireworks
Mingling with the sound of waves

19:22.078 --> 19:23.329
[sobs]

19:23.412 --> 19:27.041
I go into the shell to hear a little more

19:30.378 --> 19:32.338
I go into the shell

19:33.339 --> 19:36.467
[poetry reader] And before I realize it
I am trapped inside a cave

19:36.550 --> 19:41.764
At the sound of waves made of tears
Only the frosty moon knocks on the door

19:43.974 --> 19:46.018
Now please come on out

19:46.936 --> 19:50.272
The sky is filled with stars
Where the fireworks have faded

19:55.569 --> 19:58.072
-[sniffles]
-[music concludes]

20:15.339 --> 20:17.007
[panting]

20:17.091 --> 20:18.551
[Mi-ji and woman] Oh my gosh!

20:19.510 --> 20:22.513
Oh no! I'm so sorry.

20:29.061 --> 20:32.523
My gosh. What a coincidence
running into you here, ma'am.

20:33.691 --> 20:35.192
Did you follow me?

20:35.276 --> 20:37.570
[innocently] Did I follow you?
Of course not.

20:37.653 --> 20:40.197
I came to attend this…

20:40.281 --> 20:42.616
OVERCOME IT!
MALE MENOPAUSE HEALTH SEMINAR

20:43.325 --> 20:44.326
Ma'am?

20:44.410 --> 20:46.704
[quirky music playing]

20:48.581 --> 20:49.957
Ma'am!

20:50.040 --> 20:52.501
Ma'am, please wait! Ma'am!

20:52.585 --> 20:54.503
[indistinct chatter]

21:01.677 --> 21:04.847
[melancholic music playing]

21:08.893 --> 21:11.395
MIN YE-RIN
ADDITIONAL MATERIALS FOR J CARD

21:15.232 --> 21:16.400
[sighs]

21:37.004 --> 21:38.339
[Secretary Hwang] My gosh.

21:38.422 --> 21:40.049
Are you leaving the firm?

21:40.132 --> 21:41.175
Uh…

21:41.801 --> 21:44.804
I'm just going to organize these documents

21:44.887 --> 21:47.848
and sort these books by author.

21:47.932 --> 21:52.186
You might as well dust the top
of the bookshelf while you're at it.

21:53.437 --> 21:55.940
Oh, that's a good idea.

21:56.023 --> 21:57.107
Gosh.

21:57.650 --> 22:02.112
You're becoming a mess
because you have nothing to do.

22:02.988 --> 22:06.867
Why did you choose to join
Mr. Lee's team in the first place?

22:06.951 --> 22:10.037
Isn't he way too different from you
to be your role model?

22:12.498 --> 22:15.459
You don't make someone your role model
just because they're like you.

22:15.543 --> 22:18.420
[Secretary Hwang]
I wonder what drew you in.

22:18.504 --> 22:19.421
[scoffs]

22:19.505 --> 22:22.675
While you're cleaning, you should also
consider changing your role model.

22:22.758 --> 22:25.636
Pick another one based on
alphabetical order or something.

22:34.812 --> 22:36.522
-[sighs]
-[intriguing music playing]

22:36.605 --> 22:40.025
[host] We will invite our distinguished
alumnus, Mr. Lee Chung-gu, on stage now.

22:40.109 --> 22:42.778
Please welcome him
with a big round of applause.

22:44.947 --> 22:47.741
[music turns uplifting]

22:58.294 --> 23:00.880
2021 DISTINGUISHED ALUMNUS TALK
HNU LAW SCHOOL SEMINAR HALL

23:06.719 --> 23:08.971
-Even the shine is different.
-[music fades]

23:09.054 --> 23:11.682
They're custom-made shoes
crafted by an Italian artisan.

23:11.765 --> 23:13.309
[audience laughs]

23:14.268 --> 23:17.354
They're shoes that
poor law students can't afford.

23:17.438 --> 23:18.772
[audience laughs]

23:19.273 --> 23:20.316
But today…

23:21.108 --> 23:25.362
I'll teach you how to become an attorney
who can afford two pairs of these.

23:25.946 --> 23:28.782
[audience cheering]

23:33.621 --> 23:35.122
[Chung-gu] When you started law school,

23:35.205 --> 23:38.876
I'm sure you all had a vision of the type
of lawyer you aspired to become.

23:38.959 --> 23:40.669
Some may dream of becoming

23:40.753 --> 23:44.089
a warrior fighting for justice,
standing on the side of the weak.

23:44.173 --> 23:48.469
And I'm sure some dream of standing
on the side of the powerful

23:49.011 --> 23:50.596
to climb up the social ladder.

23:51.722 --> 23:55.225
It's not my job to decide
which side is good or evil. The key is…

23:56.101 --> 23:57.645
no matter whose side you take…

23:59.730 --> 24:00.940
you must win.

24:01.023 --> 24:02.942
[soft uplifting music playing]

24:03.025 --> 24:05.486
That is our only righteous path…

24:06.820 --> 24:08.238
and the essence of our work.

24:08.322 --> 24:10.908
[audience applauding]

24:15.204 --> 24:18.624
[interviewer] With these grades,
you must've had many job offers.

24:18.707 --> 24:21.126
But you chose our law firm

24:21.210 --> 24:24.046
just because you wanted to work
with Mr. Lee Chung-gu?

24:24.129 --> 24:26.382
-[soft uplifting music continues]
-[Ho-su] Yes, I--

24:26.465 --> 24:29.468
You must be into
"human triumph" and all that stuff.

24:30.302 --> 24:32.054
I am somewhat of an icon for that.

24:33.931 --> 24:35.849
Enough of that. [clears throat]

24:37.643 --> 24:39.228
Who do you hate?

24:40.688 --> 24:44.316
Who do you hate the most in the world?

24:47.027 --> 24:48.320
Myself.

24:57.955 --> 25:01.709
-[breathes deeply]
-[music concludes]

25:12.094 --> 25:15.055
MR. LEE CHUNG-GU

25:15.139 --> 25:16.098
YU MI-RAE

25:16.181 --> 25:18.183
[cell phone buzzing]

25:19.768 --> 25:20.978
[clears throat]

25:22.730 --> 25:23.814
Hello?

25:26.316 --> 25:27.484
So?

25:28.068 --> 25:30.279
What legal concerns
do you have about that?

25:32.531 --> 25:34.366
Is following her like that a crime?

25:34.450 --> 25:37.578
If she reports me, will I have
to stand trial and be punished?

25:37.661 --> 25:38.954
[soft quirky music playing]

25:39.038 --> 25:41.665
Did you track her location or wiretap her?

25:41.749 --> 25:44.043
Are you insane? Why would I do that?

25:44.543 --> 25:45.586
Firstly,

25:46.295 --> 25:50.841
it's not illegal to just follow her
in open areas or commonly used pathways.

25:51.675 --> 25:54.845
She could accuse you of stalking
if you were continuously following her.

25:54.928 --> 25:57.639
But following her just once
doesn't qualify as a crime.

25:57.723 --> 25:58.640
[sighs]

26:01.602 --> 26:05.147
In cases like this, the best solution…

26:06.482 --> 26:09.026
is something the law would never
recommend doing.

26:10.027 --> 26:12.029
Say sorry before things get out of hand.

26:13.197 --> 26:16.366
I've seen many people go to court
because they couldn't do that.

26:19.036 --> 26:20.537
[sighs]

26:20.621 --> 26:21.830
What?

26:22.706 --> 26:25.417
You sounded like a real lawyer just now.

26:26.460 --> 26:29.213
[scoffs] I am a real lawyer.
Did you think I was some phony?

26:29.296 --> 26:31.507
Do you have a lawyer mode?

26:32.257 --> 26:34.176
You should keep talking like that.

26:34.760 --> 26:35.886
It's cool.

26:40.682 --> 26:41.850
[music concludes]

26:41.934 --> 26:44.436
Wait, there's one more thing.
Give me that.

26:46.522 --> 26:48.273
What are the basics of an investigation?

26:48.357 --> 26:50.734
It's online research.

26:50.818 --> 26:55.531
Gather information on her
before you start following her.

26:55.614 --> 26:58.534
She's just an old lady who runs
a restaurant. I wouldn't find her online.

26:58.617 --> 27:00.077
I know this lady.

27:00.953 --> 27:02.037
What?

27:02.830 --> 27:04.373
Kim Ro-sa.
She runs a restaurant, right?

27:04.456 --> 27:05.457
RO-SA, A POET WHO COOKS

27:05.582 --> 27:06.708
She went to my school.

27:06.792 --> 27:08.502
I think she was a sociology major.

27:09.169 --> 27:10.754
She graduated from your school?

27:11.380 --> 27:14.133
Wow, she was a total elite.

27:14.216 --> 27:16.218
You don't know the poet Kim Ro-sa?

27:16.301 --> 27:17.928
"What Makes a Person Human"?

27:18.011 --> 27:20.973
That was our CSAT handwriting
confirmation phrase, remember?

27:24.059 --> 27:25.227
Handwriting…

27:26.270 --> 27:27.271
Hey.

27:28.188 --> 27:30.774
You have a good memory.
The CSAT was ages ago.

27:30.858 --> 27:32.943
THIS MONTH'S POEM
"THE SEA OF SANG-WOL" BY KIM RO-SA

27:33.026 --> 27:35.028
[gentle music playing]

27:35.112 --> 27:36.738
[Mi-ji] That poem was hers?

27:36.822 --> 27:39.283
She cried like that
after hearing her own poem?

27:39.366 --> 27:43.662
She's also famous for
the Kim Ro-sa Scholarship at our school.

27:43.745 --> 27:46.915
It's a scholarship given to new students

27:46.999 --> 27:49.209
raised by single parents
to cover the admission fees.

27:49.293 --> 27:50.669
I received it too.

27:50.752 --> 27:52.629
-You did?
-Yes.

27:53.922 --> 27:56.425
[sighs] I totally forgot about it.

27:58.468 --> 27:59.511
Gosh…

28:02.055 --> 28:04.391
[music turns quirky]

28:05.642 --> 28:08.395
Come on, Ho-su!

28:08.478 --> 28:11.064
-I don't want to.
-Why not?

28:11.148 --> 28:14.026
You said you would help me
with whatever I needed. Remember?

28:14.109 --> 28:16.653
When did I say that?
I said I'd help with whatever I can.

28:16.737 --> 28:18.947
You can go say hello, though.

28:19.031 --> 28:21.700
You said you never thanked her
after receiving the scholarship.

28:21.783 --> 28:25.287
Don't you think it's only right
to thank her personally at least once?

28:25.370 --> 28:28.498
[scoffs] You're not doing this
because it's the right thing to do.

28:28.582 --> 28:31.543
It's because of your work. Did you forget
your company is a client of ours?

28:31.627 --> 28:32.753
If we're not careful--

28:32.836 --> 28:34.796
Anyway, I can't.
It's a conflict of interest.

28:34.880 --> 28:38.133
You're just going to say hello.
How is that a conflict of interest?

28:38.217 --> 28:41.053
How would it even help if I went?

28:41.136 --> 28:44.389
She won't even remember me.
She probably doesn't even know me.

28:44.473 --> 28:48.060
Even if she doesn't remember you,
you'd be better than me right now.

28:48.143 --> 28:50.854
Let me use your school connections.

28:50.938 --> 28:52.731
-Don't be ridiculous.
-[gasps] Hey, watch out!

28:52.814 --> 28:56.068
-[music concludes]
-Isn't that illegal? He must be crazy.

28:56.610 --> 28:59.404
[gasps] Hey, Ho-su.
Are you okay? Are you hurt?

28:59.488 --> 29:01.281
No, I'm okay.

29:01.365 --> 29:04.326
You were in serious danger just now.

29:04.409 --> 29:06.119
I just saved your life.

29:07.037 --> 29:09.498
You saved my life?
You put me in greater danger.

29:09.581 --> 29:12.501
Please just help me out this once.

29:12.584 --> 29:14.503
Two heads are better than one.

29:14.586 --> 29:17.589
[sighs] Mi-rae, you and I are terrible
when it comes to people.

29:17.673 --> 29:20.509
If we both go,
it would just make things worse.

29:20.592 --> 29:22.719
If anything,
you should take Mi-ji instead.

29:22.803 --> 29:26.181
What are you talking about?
Why are you bringing her up?

29:26.265 --> 29:29.643
Mi-ji is good at getting people
to open up their hearts to her.

29:29.726 --> 29:32.312
[soft pensive music playing]

29:32.396 --> 29:35.315
[Mi-ji] I'm good at getting people
to open up their hearts?

29:36.149 --> 29:37.401
I don't know about that.

29:40.112 --> 29:42.322
-She got gold.
-[Mi-ji] Maybe the Mi-ji Ho-su remembers

29:42.406 --> 29:43.407
was like that.

29:43.490 --> 29:45.242
-[excited chatter]
-[students] Mi-ji.

29:45.325 --> 29:48.370
[Mi-ji] Even back then, I wasn't the one
who opened up people's hearts.

29:48.453 --> 29:49.621
-[student] Yu Mi-ji!
-No way.

29:49.705 --> 29:52.499
-People were just drawn to my sparkle…
-[friend] Mi-ji!

29:52.582 --> 29:54.376
…so I didn't have to do anything.

29:54.793 --> 29:56.169
-Wanna eat lunch together?
-Sure.

29:56.253 --> 29:58.797
-Okay.
-[Mi-ji] Once that sparkle disappeared…

29:58.880 --> 30:00.716
I'm supposed to go
to the bookstore with Mi-rae.

30:00.799 --> 30:03.093
I know you don't need any textbooks.

30:04.553 --> 30:05.637
Mi-rae.

30:08.432 --> 30:09.599
Let's eat lunch together.

30:09.683 --> 30:12.060
[Mi-ji] …the only thing remaining
was a burnt-out firework,

30:12.144 --> 30:15.105
useless and dull…

30:16.315 --> 30:17.691
just like me.

30:19.067 --> 30:21.778
-[soft pensive music continues]
-[camera clicking]

30:24.948 --> 30:27.409
-[lights click]
-[family] Aw!

30:34.333 --> 30:36.251
What could someone like me do?

30:37.878 --> 30:40.547
[music concludes]

30:41.757 --> 30:42.924
-[Se-jin] Hey…
-[camera clicks]

30:43.008 --> 30:45.510
Why don't we wrap things up
and finish tomorrow?

30:45.594 --> 30:46.887
You haven't even eaten yet.

30:46.970 --> 30:49.014
I'm almost done.

30:50.599 --> 30:53.060
You're very stubborn.

30:53.935 --> 30:56.688
[inhales] You remind me of someone.

30:59.316 --> 31:02.277
I'll get going now.

31:02.361 --> 31:03.737
Where are you going?

31:03.820 --> 31:05.405
I've been waiting to give you a ride.

31:05.489 --> 31:07.282
I can just walk home--

31:07.366 --> 31:10.535
Making sure my business partner
gets home safely is part of my job.

31:10.619 --> 31:11.620
Let's go.

31:12.204 --> 31:13.205
Hey, I'm leaving.

31:13.288 --> 31:15.082
[car revving]

31:17.084 --> 31:18.377
[shift lever rattling]

31:18.460 --> 31:22.089
[engine pulsing]

31:22.172 --> 31:23.507
[engine sputters, stops]

31:23.590 --> 31:25.550
[engine starts]

31:25.634 --> 31:27.677
[engine revving]

31:29.054 --> 31:30.097
-[engine stops]
-[grunts]

31:30.180 --> 31:31.390
[quirky music playing]

31:31.473 --> 31:34.059
-Why is this not moving?
-[engine starts]

31:34.142 --> 31:36.978
-[shift lever rattling]
-[engine grinding]

31:37.062 --> 31:38.522
-[Mi-rae yelps]
-[engine sputters]

31:38.605 --> 31:40.190
What the heck?

31:40.273 --> 31:42.818
Are we on a hill? Is this an incline?

31:42.901 --> 31:45.946
Instead of releasing
the clutch all the way--

31:46.029 --> 31:48.240
I know. I got my Class A license recently,

31:48.323 --> 31:50.283
so I… Wait. What's happening?

31:50.367 --> 31:51.660
Hold on! What's going on?

31:51.743 --> 31:54.746
Wait, hold on! Stop it, please!
Come on, hurry up!

31:54.830 --> 31:55.872
Stop it!

31:55.956 --> 31:57.624
[brakes squeal]

31:57.707 --> 31:59.709
[panting]

31:59.793 --> 32:01.294
-Get out.
-Yes, ma'am.

32:04.214 --> 32:05.966
-[engine revving]
-[music concludes]

32:07.342 --> 32:10.345
-[soft quirky music playing]
-[engine revving smoothly]

32:12.097 --> 32:15.350
How are you so good at driving
when you can't even ride a bike?

32:15.434 --> 32:18.019
You use your body
to learn how to ride a bike.

32:18.103 --> 32:19.855
But you need to pass a test to drive.

32:19.938 --> 32:21.773
So you're good at tests.

32:22.607 --> 32:23.817
Maybe that's why?

32:24.359 --> 32:26.486
You sounded just like
a driving test examiner earlier.

32:26.570 --> 32:29.489
The brake, and then, "Get out."
I was totally traumatized.

32:30.240 --> 32:32.659
But why do you insist on driving a manual?

32:32.742 --> 32:34.327
There are automatic trucks.

32:35.120 --> 32:37.497
Because it looks cool.
It also reminds me of Mad Max.

32:37.581 --> 32:40.167
-[imitates spray can hissing]
-[heavy metal music playing]

32:40.250 --> 32:41.293
[sighs]

32:44.171 --> 32:45.797
[engine revs]

32:48.967 --> 32:50.427
[music concludes]

32:50.510 --> 32:51.761
[engine stops]

33:00.061 --> 33:03.523
Are you sure you can drive back?

33:03.607 --> 33:05.734
I'm going to call a driver.

33:05.817 --> 33:06.943
I see.

33:08.528 --> 33:10.280
What time should we meet tomorrow?

33:10.363 --> 33:13.742
I need to go to
my grandmother's hospital tomorrow.

33:13.825 --> 33:17.120
I see. Then I'll do
the remaining work by myself.

33:17.204 --> 33:20.457
I think I can work the day
after tomorrow. Let's do it together.

33:20.540 --> 33:22.459
No, don't push yourself. I can do it.

33:22.542 --> 33:26.046
We agreed to work on it together,
so I'm responsible too.

33:26.129 --> 33:27.422
See you in two days.

33:28.215 --> 33:29.132
Now, I remember.

33:30.091 --> 33:31.301
Pardon?

33:31.384 --> 33:33.720
I thought you reminded me of someone.

33:34.888 --> 33:36.348
I'll tell you later.

33:36.431 --> 33:38.767
Anyway, see you the day after tomorrow.

33:38.850 --> 33:40.435
Yes, goodbye.

33:45.440 --> 33:46.816
Excuse me, Mi-hye.

33:46.900 --> 33:48.652
[suspenseful quirky music playing]

33:48.735 --> 33:49.903
[sighs]

34:01.623 --> 34:04.376
You forgot your pay for today.

34:05.168 --> 34:06.211
Ah.

34:10.423 --> 34:11.716
[softly] Thank you.

34:12.300 --> 34:14.636
-Thank you.
-No, thank you.

34:16.888 --> 34:18.348
Get home safe.

34:19.015 --> 34:20.308
-Goodbye.
-[gate opens]

34:21.726 --> 34:22.769
[gate closes]

34:25.772 --> 34:26.856
Jeez…

34:29.526 --> 34:31.027
Where am I?

34:31.111 --> 34:32.988
Can a driver come at this hour?

34:33.071 --> 34:35.991
Are there people who ask for one
even when they're not drunk?

34:39.327 --> 34:40.495
[music concludes]

34:40.579 --> 34:41.830
[Ro-sa muttering]

34:41.913 --> 34:42.998
[Mi-ji] Excuse me…

34:43.957 --> 34:45.166
This is for you.

34:45.250 --> 34:47.335
-[Ro-sa] What is that?
-[bubbles burbling]

34:48.461 --> 34:49.963
In yesterday's poem,

34:50.630 --> 34:54.342
I liked the line about
the sound of waves, so I brought this.

34:56.011 --> 34:58.388
I don't know much about poems.

34:58.471 --> 35:01.725
But I felt like the poem was speaking
on your behalf.

35:03.810 --> 35:05.604
So is that a bribe?

35:05.687 --> 35:08.023
No, it's not a bribe.

35:09.691 --> 35:11.234
It's an apology.

35:11.318 --> 35:14.404
I'm sorry I was
following you around yesterday.

35:15.155 --> 35:16.239
Well…

35:17.866 --> 35:21.411
I heard you wrote that poem.

35:21.494 --> 35:25.457
I had no idea
that you were such a famous poet.

35:25.540 --> 35:28.084
I also heard that you majored
in sociology at HNU.

35:28.627 --> 35:31.713
And that you've been sponsoring
scholarships for a while. You're amazing--

35:31.796 --> 35:34.049
First you follow me,
and now you do a background check?

35:34.132 --> 35:35.425
No, ma'am.

35:35.508 --> 35:38.219
I wasn't doing that. Someone just told me.

35:38.928 --> 35:42.223
I found out that my friend
was a recipient of your scholarship.

35:42.307 --> 35:44.351
Although it was a long time ago.

35:44.434 --> 35:45.352
Your friend?

35:45.435 --> 35:47.812
Yes, my friend.

35:47.896 --> 35:50.565
He's the same age as me,
but he graduated from HNU.

35:50.649 --> 35:54.361
[gasps] He's now an attorney
for a very famous law firm.

35:54.444 --> 35:56.363
He told me that it's all thanks to you.

35:56.446 --> 35:59.240
[sighs] Admission fees
don't even cost that much.

35:59.324 --> 36:01.117
He got there on his own.

36:01.201 --> 36:03.411
No, he said he feels
really grateful to you.

36:03.495 --> 36:05.664
He wants to come thank you in person…

36:05.747 --> 36:07.832
He wants to come and say hello? Here?

36:09.334 --> 36:12.671
Well… Right now…

36:12.754 --> 36:15.590
He has a lot going on,
so he can't come right away.

36:15.674 --> 36:18.927
But he said he really wanted to come.
But his company is--

36:19.010 --> 36:20.178
Forget it.

36:21.971 --> 36:25.141
No one ever came and thanked me anyway.

36:25.892 --> 36:27.143
[Mi-ji] Oh.

36:27.227 --> 36:29.270
That must've made you sad.

36:30.063 --> 36:31.648
Why would I feel sad over that?

36:31.731 --> 36:34.359
I'm just repaying the school.

36:35.151 --> 36:38.613
Even so, it's sad when people
don't reciprocate how you feel.

36:39.155 --> 36:40.490
Donating is not easy either.

36:40.573 --> 36:41.866
[Ro-sa] It's better this way.

36:41.950 --> 36:46.246
Only people who still need something
come with things like that.

36:46.955 --> 36:48.957
No, this isn't because I need something.

36:49.040 --> 36:51.167
That poem really touched me.

36:53.420 --> 36:54.754
Should I throw it away?

36:58.383 --> 37:00.343
[tender music playing]

37:00.427 --> 37:02.303
-My goodness…
-[cell phone buzzing]

37:06.850 --> 37:09.519
[cell phone buzzing]

37:12.689 --> 37:14.065
Hello?

37:14.899 --> 37:17.944
It took you long enough.
I called you ages ago.

37:18.027 --> 37:20.822
You swore that you were going
to send someone today.

37:20.905 --> 37:24.367
If you keep this up, I'll have no choice
but to change cleaning companies.

37:24.451 --> 37:25.452
Ah…

37:26.578 --> 37:29.748
I get that you're busy,
but I can't stand it any longer.

37:29.831 --> 37:32.167
At this rate,
I'm going to pay more in hospital bills

37:32.250 --> 37:34.627
from having to go up
and down the stairs to clean.

37:35.253 --> 37:36.588
[Mi-ji] Ma'am.

37:36.671 --> 37:37.839
May I use the restroom?

37:39.758 --> 37:41.426
So when are you going to send someone?

37:43.136 --> 37:45.263
[music turns uplifting]

37:49.350 --> 37:51.060
-[door lock rattling]
-[door opens]

37:54.147 --> 37:55.607
[Mi-ji] Mm…

37:58.026 --> 38:00.278
-This is my field of expertise.
-[music concludes]

38:01.696 --> 38:05.074
So you're saying you can't make it
to work tomorrow, right?

38:05.867 --> 38:08.161
Why were you beating around the bush?

38:08.244 --> 38:09.704
It's your mother.

38:09.788 --> 38:11.956
My absence from work yesterday
was also unexpected.

38:12.040 --> 38:14.042
I feel bad that I keep skipping work.

38:16.503 --> 38:19.756
This is all because of Mi-ji.

38:20.256 --> 38:22.425
She used to drop everything
to go see her grandma,

38:22.509 --> 38:24.677
but something's gotten into her lately.

38:24.761 --> 38:28.473
-As if her so-called job is important.
-You shouldn't say things like that.

38:29.265 --> 38:32.227
Hey, Mi-ji is her granddaughter.

38:32.310 --> 38:33.812
Look at other families.

38:33.895 --> 38:37.023
Some kids get credit just for visiting
their grandparents during holidays.

38:37.106 --> 38:40.193
No other granddaughter
takes care of her sick grandmother.

38:40.276 --> 38:42.237
You've had it easy until now
thanks to Mi-ji.

38:42.320 --> 38:44.823
Are you really complaining
because she's not doing that now?

38:44.906 --> 38:46.616
You're right.

38:46.699 --> 38:49.661
But she's always been so close
to her grandma.

38:49.744 --> 38:51.788
She can't be as close to her
as her own daughter.

38:51.871 --> 38:53.164
Be good to your mom.

38:53.248 --> 38:54.499
Work should not come first.

39:01.130 --> 39:04.676
That's why I said I can't work tomorrow.
I'll be taking care of her.

39:05.802 --> 39:08.221
There you go again, twisting my words.

39:09.347 --> 39:12.809
Just think of it as a chance to repay her
for all the love she's given you.

39:12.892 --> 39:15.562
-[Ok-hui] Jeez.
-You should repay everything.

39:15.645 --> 39:17.313
Or you're going to regret it.

39:17.397 --> 39:18.481
Hey.

39:19.524 --> 39:20.650
What would you know?

39:21.359 --> 39:23.111
Not everyone is like you and your mom.

39:23.945 --> 39:26.698
My mom was cast aside
for giving birth to a daughter,

39:26.781 --> 39:29.242
while your mom bought you
new clothes every year.

39:29.325 --> 39:32.120
Why don't you repay your mom for all she's
done while she's still alive?

39:32.203 --> 39:35.748
I wasn't that cherished compared to you,
so I don't owe her that much.

39:36.749 --> 39:39.210
I'm coming to work tomorrow.
And that's final.

39:40.086 --> 39:42.964
[pensive music playing]

39:51.723 --> 39:54.601
[loudly] What do you mean
you want me to hand over J Card?

39:55.184 --> 39:56.853
Ma'am, this really isn't right.

39:56.936 --> 39:58.980
I've been in charge of it
from the beginning.

39:59.063 --> 40:02.984
-More than anyone else, I--
-[whispers] It was Mr. Lee's order.

40:09.824 --> 40:10.825
[sighs]

40:17.582 --> 40:20.668
When are we leaving for the meeting?
Their headquarters is in Gangnam, right?

40:20.752 --> 40:22.420
No, it's Jonggak.
We should leave soon if--

40:22.503 --> 40:23.630
I want to go too.

40:24.213 --> 40:25.423
-What?
-[music concludes]

40:25.506 --> 40:27.634
I said I'm going
to the J Card meeting too.

40:28.468 --> 40:32.096
You two just got the documents.
You haven't even had time to read them.

40:32.722 --> 40:34.557
I know them better than anyone. Let me go.

40:34.641 --> 40:36.392
-Even so, this is out of the blue--
-Stop.

40:36.476 --> 40:38.019
Are you that desperate, Ho-su?

40:38.770 --> 40:40.521
Desperate enough to insist on joining us?

40:40.605 --> 40:41.564
[Ho-su] Yes.

40:42.231 --> 40:44.901
Then get ready to go.
We're leaving right away.

40:52.200 --> 40:53.368
[sighs]

40:53.451 --> 40:56.037
Is the toilet clogged again?

41:04.379 --> 41:05.463
Huh?

41:05.964 --> 41:07.215
[Mi-ji exhales]

41:10.176 --> 41:11.427
What are you doing?

41:11.511 --> 41:14.472
I'm almost done.
I just need to get to the bottom and--

41:14.555 --> 41:16.641
I asked you a question!

41:16.724 --> 41:19.435
Pardon? I'm cleaning.

41:19.519 --> 41:21.229
Did I tell you to do that?

41:22.063 --> 41:25.650
I overheard you talking earlier,

41:25.733 --> 41:28.319
and it seemed like you needed a hand.

41:28.403 --> 41:30.655
I'm sorry if I upset you.

41:30.738 --> 41:33.533
Did your company tell you
to do things like this?

41:33.616 --> 41:36.119
No, not really.

41:36.202 --> 41:40.164
So why are you doing something
your company and I never told you to do?

41:41.207 --> 41:42.333
I…

41:45.253 --> 41:48.673
Because I don't know what to do…

41:49.590 --> 41:50.633
What?

41:50.717 --> 41:54.220
I want to get on your good side,

41:54.303 --> 41:56.347
but I don't know how.

41:56.431 --> 41:59.684
But this is something I can do…

42:01.352 --> 42:02.437
I'm sorry.

42:06.607 --> 42:09.652
[melancholic music playing]

42:18.036 --> 42:19.203
[exhales]

42:20.246 --> 42:22.331
How is it that even after decades

42:22.999 --> 42:26.961
they're still trying to use a kid
to do their dirty work?

42:29.922 --> 42:31.507
Don't ever come back here.

42:32.341 --> 42:35.678
I detest that company,
so I have no intention of selling my land.

42:35.762 --> 42:37.055
But ma'am--

42:37.138 --> 42:38.723
If you come back again,

42:39.515 --> 42:42.310
I will take it up with your company.

42:44.896 --> 42:46.064
I…

42:48.274 --> 42:49.567
It closed. [sighs]

42:49.734 --> 42:51.944
[melancholic music continues]

43:00.495 --> 43:01.579
[sighs]

43:06.125 --> 43:07.627
Mom!

43:07.710 --> 43:09.545
Mom, look at me!

43:11.380 --> 43:12.757
Mom, look at this!

43:13.883 --> 43:15.885
-Hey, Ho-su.
-[music fades]

43:15.968 --> 43:17.720
You better come and cheer me on tomorrow.

43:17.804 --> 43:19.931
I need to tell you something if I win.

43:20.014 --> 43:21.849
[young Mi-ji] Mom, look at me.

43:21.933 --> 43:23.726
Mi-ji, wait. Hear me out.

43:23.810 --> 43:26.479
-I couldn't go yesterday because--
-You came, though.

43:26.562 --> 43:29.690
You came and left with Mi-rae. Am I wrong?

43:29.774 --> 43:31.692
[somber music playing]

43:33.945 --> 43:35.071
You're right.

43:36.823 --> 43:38.866
[breathing heavily]

43:39.492 --> 43:40.701
[Mi-ji] It closed.

43:49.919 --> 43:52.130
I like you, Mi-ji.

43:52.213 --> 43:54.674
Go out with me.

43:58.261 --> 43:59.303
Fine.

44:00.471 --> 44:01.472
What?

44:03.432 --> 44:06.352
Hey, Mi-ji! Wait for me!

44:06.435 --> 44:08.479
[young Mi-ji]
Mom! I asked you to look at me.

44:08.563 --> 44:10.106
[somber music continues]

44:12.358 --> 44:14.110
[breathes deeply]

44:19.240 --> 44:21.284
[panting]

44:21.909 --> 44:23.077
[inhales sharply]

44:23.744 --> 44:24.829
[groans]

44:26.622 --> 44:29.667
Hey, Mi-ji.
Why did you take off your cast already?

44:29.793 --> 44:31.843
-I'm all better.
-You idiot.

44:32.793 --> 44:35.047
Resting is part of training too.

44:35.131 --> 44:38.759
-Proper rehabilitation is--
-I need to get into college this year.

44:39.343 --> 44:41.053
I need to be in the fall meet.

44:46.684 --> 44:47.768
[groans]

44:47.852 --> 44:48.936
My goodness.

44:49.020 --> 44:50.688
[music fades]

44:52.231 --> 44:54.358
I'm afraid she can't continue
as an athlete.

44:54.442 --> 44:56.777
-Oh dear.
-My gosh.

44:56.861 --> 44:58.905
That idiot.

44:58.988 --> 45:01.282
I knew this would happen
when she wouldn't listen.

45:01.365 --> 45:03.868
-How is she going to make a living now?
-[Wol-sun] Quiet down!

45:03.951 --> 45:05.953
-[Ok-hui] Let's go already!
-[Wol-sun] Hold on!

45:06.037 --> 45:08.206
-[Ok-hui] He just said she can't run!
-[Mi-ji] It closed.

45:08.289 --> 45:12.126
Mom, I can do it hands-free.
Mom, I'm going to let go!

45:13.419 --> 45:17.006
-[grunts]
-Mi-ji, I told you to stay still.

45:17.089 --> 45:18.799
Your sister's tired.
Let's hurry up and go.

45:18.883 --> 45:20.676
[melancholic music playing]

45:26.140 --> 45:28.309
[melancholic music continues]

45:33.231 --> 45:36.567
I should've just stayed still.

45:39.153 --> 45:41.155
[breathes deeply]

45:41.239 --> 45:43.699
[music fades]

45:43.783 --> 45:46.285
[colleague] I'm sorry
that we suddenly added another person.

45:46.369 --> 45:48.246
-Thank you.
-Don't mention it.

45:48.329 --> 45:50.998
We're grateful that you came
to a place near our office. [chuckles]

45:51.082 --> 45:54.335
By the way, is he usually that quiet?

45:54.418 --> 45:55.711
Was he forced to come?

45:55.795 --> 45:59.257
Don't let him fool you. He's just
pretending to be the silent, cool guy.

45:59.340 --> 46:00.800
It's just for show.

46:01.384 --> 46:03.261
Where's the other lady?

46:03.344 --> 46:06.013
I guess she's wrapping up work
and running late.

46:06.097 --> 46:09.225
We had to urgently get someone
who hadn't left work yet.

46:09.976 --> 46:11.060
I'm leaving.

46:12.186 --> 46:13.312
Hey, where are you going?

46:13.396 --> 46:15.982
We barely managed
to get an even number of people.

46:16.065 --> 46:17.400
We'll talk tomorrow.

46:23.698 --> 46:24.824
[woman] Oh?

46:25.950 --> 46:26.951
Ho-su?

46:31.122 --> 46:33.374
[cell phone buzzing]

46:41.632 --> 46:42.800
[clears throat]

46:43.676 --> 46:44.719
What is it?

46:45.386 --> 46:46.637
I'm on the bus.

46:48.097 --> 46:50.391
No, I'm on my way home.

46:53.352 --> 46:54.520
Right now?

46:56.939 --> 47:00.985
Well, I am in the area.

47:14.915 --> 47:17.209
Wow, it's so big.

47:23.841 --> 47:25.426
[Ho-su] Over here, Mi-rae.

47:28.512 --> 47:32.892
Hey, Mi-rae. It's been a while.
How have you been?

47:33.768 --> 47:35.978
Hey, Ji-yun.

47:36.062 --> 47:37.146
[young Ji-yun] Mi-ji!

47:37.229 --> 47:40.066
-[pensive music playing]
-Want to eat lunch together?

47:40.941 --> 47:42.026
Mi-rae!

47:46.447 --> 47:48.157
[music fades]

47:48.240 --> 47:51.118
Why did you call me
when you were with her?

47:51.827 --> 47:53.287
You two are close.

47:54.121 --> 47:57.833
It's been a while since she last saw you,
so she wanted to meet up.

47:57.917 --> 47:59.960
She said it's been a while
since she saw me?

48:00.044 --> 48:01.128
Yes.

48:04.590 --> 48:06.092
What were you two talking about?

48:06.175 --> 48:07.718
Nothing.

48:09.345 --> 48:11.389
How did you two run into each other?

48:11.472 --> 48:14.100
-It was nothing. Just earlier--
-Don't even get me started.

48:14.183 --> 48:16.018
I thought we were in a sitcom.

48:16.519 --> 48:20.481
Ho-su showed up to a triple blind date
thinking it was a business meeting.

48:20.564 --> 48:23.526
[chuckles]
How can a lawyer be so naive?

48:24.318 --> 48:27.613
He's always been like that.
That's why he's just so interesting.

48:28.739 --> 48:30.699
-Don't you agree, Mi-rae?
-[pensive music playing]

48:30.783 --> 48:33.119
[Mi-ji] You mean you find it
interesting that he's a lawyer.

48:33.202 --> 48:36.705
Oh, right. Are you still working
at that public corporation, Mi-rae?

48:36.789 --> 48:38.624
Yes. What about you, Ji-yun?

48:38.707 --> 48:40.418
Didn't I tell you?

48:40.501 --> 48:42.711
My office is near here. It's J Card.

48:42.795 --> 48:44.547
Have you heard of Gourmet Guide?

48:45.297 --> 48:47.091
-Gour… what?
-[Ji-yun] You don't know it?

48:47.174 --> 48:51.262
Famous restaurants usually have it
on a sign out front. You've never seen it?

48:51.345 --> 48:54.598
We select popular restaurants
and create content.

48:55.808 --> 48:57.810
Basically, we help discover
popular restaurants.

48:57.893 --> 48:58.894
[chuckles softly]

48:58.978 --> 49:02.898
[chuckles] By the way, Ho-su,
you said you work for Wongeun Law firm.

49:02.982 --> 49:04.150
Then do you know Beauer?

49:04.233 --> 49:06.819
It's one of the candidate restaurants
for this season.

49:06.902 --> 49:08.487
[Ho-su] Yes, I've been there a few times.

49:08.571 --> 49:10.614
My gosh. How did you get a reservation?

49:10.698 --> 49:12.450
The owner is a client of ours.

49:12.533 --> 49:15.786
Does that mean I can make
a reservation through you?

49:16.328 --> 49:19.165
Sure. I'll give them a call tomorrow.

49:19.248 --> 49:20.332
[Ji-yun] Really?

49:20.416 --> 49:21.500
[chuckles]

49:22.626 --> 49:24.295
[music fades]

49:26.922 --> 49:29.550
-[sighs deeply]
-Ho-su and I are headed the same way.

49:29.633 --> 49:31.218
You're going home too, right?

49:31.302 --> 49:32.636
What?

49:32.720 --> 49:36.056
I'm going to stop by Aesim-dong.

49:36.140 --> 49:37.975
Aesim-dong? Now?

49:38.809 --> 49:41.604
Yes, something just came up.

49:42.229 --> 49:45.191
If you're going there,
then we can take the subway together.

49:45.274 --> 49:47.151
Ho-su, I can drop you off on my way home.

49:47.234 --> 49:48.569
I brought my car.

49:48.652 --> 49:50.196
You drank, though.

49:50.279 --> 49:51.947
It was non-alcoholic.

49:53.365 --> 49:55.701
I see. You know, Aesim-dong
is in the same direction.

49:55.784 --> 49:57.620
Can you drop me off too?

49:57.703 --> 50:00.623
Aesim-dong is a bit too far.

50:00.706 --> 50:03.083
I think I'll hit traffic on my way back.

50:04.001 --> 50:05.252
I see.

50:06.086 --> 50:08.422
We wouldn't want that. [chuckles]

50:08.506 --> 50:11.634
Ho-su, don't be a burden
and just ride the subway with me.

50:12.968 --> 50:14.428
I don't mind, though.

50:15.888 --> 50:19.600
Ho-su, it's up to you.
What do you want to do?

50:24.146 --> 50:27.608
[Mi-ji] Come with me. Me!

50:31.278 --> 50:34.365
I heard some people find
public corporations too conservative.

50:35.366 --> 50:36.992
But I guess you're fine with it.

50:38.536 --> 50:40.871
No one works at a company
because it suits them.

50:40.955 --> 50:43.791
[inhales]
We all just work to make a living.

50:43.874 --> 50:47.795
That's true. You weren't even thinking
of working there in the first place.

50:47.878 --> 50:49.380
You really lowered your standards

50:49.463 --> 50:51.507
for someone who studied
for the civil service exam.

50:51.590 --> 50:53.259
[tense quirky music playing]

50:53.968 --> 50:55.719
How is J Card?

50:56.679 --> 50:58.264
Were you always interested in that field?

50:58.347 --> 51:00.683
[chuckles]

51:02.726 --> 51:04.144
How's Mi-ji?

51:04.770 --> 51:07.731
Seeing you like this makes me
want to see Mi-ji. I miss her.

51:08.232 --> 51:11.235
[chuckles] What's the point?
It would just be awkward.

51:11.318 --> 51:14.446
Why? You know
I was Mi-ji's number one fan.

51:15.447 --> 51:17.616
She did keep her distance from me, though.

51:19.201 --> 51:21.287
When did she ever do that?

51:21.370 --> 51:22.746
You must've done that first.

51:22.830 --> 51:25.374
What? [chuckles]

51:25.457 --> 51:27.042
Don't you remember?

51:27.126 --> 51:31.130
In the past, I used to ask you
what Mi-ji thought of me.

51:31.880 --> 51:34.717
[sighs] I don't know
what I did to upset her.

51:35.759 --> 51:38.012
Why did she suddenly
distance herself from me?

51:41.599 --> 51:42.683
My gosh.

51:43.309 --> 51:44.727
You haven't changed.

51:44.810 --> 51:47.313
You never listen to me, do you?
Not then, and not now.

51:47.396 --> 51:48.897
[chuckles]

51:51.317 --> 51:55.696
CHICKEN GIBLET STEW

51:55.821 --> 51:57.448
[music fades]

51:57.531 --> 52:00.909
Oh, is it this restaurant?
But why'd you come here at this hour?

52:01.327 --> 52:05.164
I accidentally took something
earlier today, so I came to return it.

52:05.247 --> 52:07.041
Why did you come here during the day?

52:07.124 --> 52:09.001
You don't usually work outside the office.

52:09.084 --> 52:10.127
Well…

52:10.753 --> 52:13.213
I took half a day off to help someone.

52:14.423 --> 52:16.925
You barely have enough time
to even meet like this.

52:17.468 --> 52:19.470
I can't believe you took time off.
Who was it?

52:19.553 --> 52:21.513
A relative.

52:21.597 --> 52:24.058
My great-aunt asked me
to look after her place for a while.

52:24.141 --> 52:27.144
But I accidentally took
the restroom key with me.

52:27.227 --> 52:29.813
This is your great-aunt's restaurant?

52:29.897 --> 52:31.440
I think I've heard of this place before.

52:31.523 --> 52:33.567
Thanks so much for the ride.

52:34.276 --> 52:36.570
Take care. See you.

52:36.654 --> 52:37.738
Bye.

52:44.495 --> 52:47.539
AESIM-DONG REDEVELOPMENT
PROMOTION COMMITTEE

52:48.165 --> 52:50.751
Jeez, that felt like an interrogation.

52:52.753 --> 52:55.005
Why did I pretend that
she's my great-aunt of all things?

52:55.089 --> 52:56.048
[clicks tongue]

52:56.131 --> 52:58.425
Whatever. I won't see her again anyway.

53:01.470 --> 53:02.596
[mutters]

53:02.680 --> 53:05.516
-[heartbeat thumping]
-[tender music playing]

53:05.599 --> 53:06.934
[sighs]

53:07.017 --> 53:10.229
Why was she looking at me like that?
I keep thinking about her.

53:14.316 --> 53:15.442
[grunts]

53:15.526 --> 53:16.694
[music fades]

53:16.777 --> 53:18.570
I just feel guilty. That's all.

53:19.154 --> 53:22.991
I'm just feeling guilty
about that whistleblowing case.

53:23.075 --> 53:26.161
-[breathes deeply]
-[quirky music playing]

53:26.245 --> 53:27.371
[Ho-su grunts]

53:30.499 --> 53:32.084
[music fades]

53:34.044 --> 53:35.462
[in English] Hi.

53:35.546 --> 53:38.841
[in Korean] Why are you by yourself?
Did Mi-ji run away already?

53:39.883 --> 53:41.510
-Take that back and hurry up.
-Fine.

53:41.593 --> 53:43.387
Words have power.

53:43.929 --> 53:46.140
It's fine. Just hurry up
and go clean the storage room.

53:46.223 --> 53:48.475
I'm going to leave
after I help you move this.

53:48.976 --> 53:50.060
Move aside.

53:52.813 --> 53:54.022
[Se-jin groans]

53:58.569 --> 54:00.028
[soft pensive music playing]

54:00.112 --> 54:01.155
[Se-jin] What's this?

54:07.453 --> 54:11.623
What the heck?
When did you organize all this?

54:11.707 --> 54:12.750
Huh?

54:13.375 --> 54:14.376
I know, right?

54:16.003 --> 54:18.338
Have you finally
pulled yourself together, Se-jin?

54:18.422 --> 54:19.506
[chuckles]

54:25.012 --> 54:26.722
I didn't mean cleaning, you know?

54:26.805 --> 54:28.265
You're dodging the issue.

54:29.224 --> 54:32.227
[Mi-rae] But you just leave me hanging
and judge me however you like.

54:32.311 --> 54:33.812
It's like playing with a bug,

54:33.896 --> 54:36.398
pulling off its legs
just to see how long it lasts.

54:36.482 --> 54:38.817
You really find that fun?
Why are you so cruel?

54:38.901 --> 54:40.861
How could you treat someone like that?

54:44.364 --> 54:46.450
[music fades]

54:57.503 --> 54:59.004
I'm sorry for the surprise call.

54:59.087 --> 55:01.048
I want to introduce someone to you.

55:01.715 --> 55:02.925
Introduce someone?

55:03.926 --> 55:05.594
Here he comes. Over here.

55:08.472 --> 55:09.932
You've seen him on TV, right?

55:10.015 --> 55:13.560
Meet Mr. Yun Ji-sang,
Wongeun's one and only humanist lawyer.

55:13.644 --> 55:14.645
Oh, come on.

55:14.728 --> 55:17.356
I've heard a lot about you.
My name is Yun Ji-sang.

55:17.439 --> 55:18.857
Hello.

55:19.441 --> 55:20.818
My name is Lee Ho-su.

55:20.901 --> 55:22.528
I heard that you're good at your job.

55:22.611 --> 55:24.404
But since you're a junior
Chung-gu cares about,

55:24.488 --> 55:26.698
I thought you weren't interested
in public interest cases.

55:26.782 --> 55:29.827
You know how much he hates those cases.

55:29.910 --> 55:32.162
[laughs]

55:33.121 --> 55:36.375
So, how long have you been
interested in our team?

55:37.000 --> 55:40.045
[intriguing music playing]

55:54.351 --> 55:55.477
What is it?

55:59.773 --> 56:01.608
Why are you doing this to me, sir?

56:02.776 --> 56:05.821
Why are you suddenly telling me
to go to another team?

56:05.904 --> 56:09.908
It may feel out of the blue,
but Mr. Yun is a really great guy.

56:09.992 --> 56:12.953
It's hard to stay true to your principles
and still be good at your job.

56:13.036 --> 56:15.080
And in terms of that field, he's way--

56:15.163 --> 56:17.207
-Mr. Lee.
-[music concludes]

56:19.835 --> 56:24.172
Whenever you see someone
weak, powerless, or pitiful…

56:26.049 --> 56:27.926
you can never turn a blind eye.

56:29.261 --> 56:31.972
Given your tendency to prioritize
protecting the weak over your team,

56:32.055 --> 56:34.683
isn't the Corporate Social
Responsibility Team a better fit for you?

56:34.766 --> 56:36.518
I don't want to go to another team.

56:37.436 --> 56:38.478
Why not?

56:40.355 --> 56:42.774
Because other people don't have
a disability like I do?

56:43.901 --> 56:45.068
[pensive music playing]

56:45.152 --> 56:46.278
Pardon?

56:50.824 --> 56:52.159
You know…

56:53.368 --> 56:55.120
I thought you wanted to become stronger.

56:55.203 --> 56:57.331
And I thought that
was what made you like me,

56:57.414 --> 57:01.001
not the disability
or your workaholic tendency.

57:01.710 --> 57:05.047
But after what happened recently,
I realized something.

57:06.673 --> 57:09.009
I wanted to keep you by my side
because of your strengths,

57:09.092 --> 57:14.681
but you were by my side
because of my weakness.

57:16.558 --> 57:20.187
However, I absolutely hate that.

57:24.191 --> 57:25.859
[wheelchair joystick clicking]

57:33.075 --> 57:34.284
Is that…

57:36.870 --> 57:37.871
so terrible?

57:38.789 --> 57:41.166
-[inhales] Mm.
-[music fades]

57:42.417 --> 57:45.170
I think what you perceive
as your weakness…

57:47.631 --> 57:50.884
is what makes you stronger and special.

57:52.636 --> 57:55.097
I'm drawn to you
because I see your vulnerability,

57:55.973 --> 57:59.851
and I admire you even more
because of that weakness.

58:02.270 --> 58:04.022
Is that so terrible?

58:05.315 --> 58:06.441
[chuckles]

58:07.943 --> 58:09.653
[pensive music playing]

58:10.404 --> 58:12.280
Chairman Choi's victim…

58:13.532 --> 58:16.201
You helped him, didn't you?
Why did you do that?

58:16.284 --> 58:19.162
I didn't help him.
I just told him the rules.

58:20.706 --> 58:23.291
It's unfair to throw someone
into the ring

58:23.792 --> 58:27.129
when they don't even know
how to put on gloves or a mouthguard.

58:27.212 --> 58:30.257
I believed we could win
without going to such lengths.

58:30.340 --> 58:32.801
But you can't just blindside me
without saying a word.

58:32.884 --> 58:36.263
[inhales] Is that your definition
of a professional?

58:38.598 --> 58:41.309
No matter what excuse you give
to justify your actions,

58:41.852 --> 58:43.979
it's still a breach of trust
to the company

58:44.646 --> 58:45.772
and a betrayal to me.

58:47.649 --> 58:48.734
I'm sorry.

58:48.817 --> 58:50.527
[breathes deeply]

58:51.528 --> 58:55.032
I regret acting alone
without discussing it with you.

59:01.997 --> 59:03.248
[Chung-gu groans]

59:05.250 --> 59:06.334
[grunts]

59:09.129 --> 59:10.881
Make a decision now.

59:12.549 --> 59:16.261
Are you certain that you want
to continue working with me?

59:17.763 --> 59:18.680
Yes, sir.

59:21.850 --> 59:24.686
I'm supposed to have a drink
with Chairman Choi later.

59:25.979 --> 59:27.272
What do you say?

59:28.356 --> 59:29.775
Would you like to join this time?

59:35.614 --> 59:36.615
[music concludes]

59:36.698 --> 59:38.575
LAND ACQUISITION BUSINESS PROPOSAL

59:39.451 --> 59:40.660
[sighs]

59:42.913 --> 59:44.122
[footsteps approaching]

59:49.711 --> 59:50.796
Oh.

59:51.963 --> 59:55.050
You look tired. How's work going?

59:55.133 --> 59:58.386
[chuckles] I'm trying my best, sir.

59:58.470 --> 01:00:00.097
Don't push yourself too hard.

01:00:00.931 --> 01:00:04.392
By the way, how about a meeting
with the landowner next week?

01:00:04.976 --> 01:00:05.894
Pardon?

01:00:05.977 --> 01:00:08.313
-Next week?
-Yes.

01:00:08.396 --> 01:00:11.483
Find out which day works best for her
and bring her next week.

01:00:12.025 --> 01:00:15.821
I know you've been working hard,
so that wouldn't be a hard ask, right?

01:00:15.904 --> 01:00:18.031
[tense music playing]

01:00:18.115 --> 01:00:20.784
Still, next week is a bit--

01:00:20.867 --> 01:00:23.787
I told them
that the schedule is too tight,

01:00:23.870 --> 01:00:26.957
but the General Affairs Team keep
hounding me about the site issue.

01:00:27.040 --> 01:00:29.292
They're concerned
about their performance too.

01:00:29.876 --> 01:00:32.420
This performance review
is really important.

01:00:34.172 --> 01:00:35.924
I trust that
you'll bring her in next week.

01:00:36.007 --> 01:00:38.343
Pardon? But…

01:00:38.426 --> 01:00:39.636
Sir…

01:00:40.387 --> 01:00:41.513
[sighs]

01:00:50.939 --> 01:00:53.441
-[sighs heavily]
-[music concludes]

01:00:53.525 --> 01:00:57.571
[Mi-ji] How am I supposed
to bring her to the office

01:00:57.654 --> 01:01:01.408
when she told me
not to even come to her restaurant?

01:01:04.286 --> 01:01:06.955
I wonder if they'd take pity on me
if a bus grazes me.

01:01:08.790 --> 01:01:11.835
Maybe they'd at least postpone
the meeting until I'm discharged.

01:01:11.918 --> 01:01:13.628
[whimpers]

01:01:14.337 --> 01:01:15.463
[employee] Excuse me.

01:01:18.925 --> 01:01:20.135
Are you okay?

01:01:23.638 --> 01:01:26.057
Who? Me?

01:01:27.225 --> 01:01:28.643
Yes.

01:01:28.727 --> 01:01:30.395
I guess so.

01:01:35.525 --> 01:01:38.737
What was that about?
Did he hear what I said?

01:01:38.820 --> 01:01:42.324
[groans] Did I look that miserable?

01:01:44.201 --> 01:01:46.077
-[sighs]
-[cell phone buzzing]

01:01:50.290 --> 01:01:51.917
[groans] Why is she calling?

01:01:52.000 --> 01:01:52.876
PARK JI-YUN

01:01:58.173 --> 01:02:00.091
Are you for real?

01:02:04.137 --> 01:02:06.514
-Hello?
-[Ji-yun] Are you busy, Mi-rae?

01:02:06.598 --> 01:02:10.227
-Can you talk right now?
-I'm in the middle of work. What is it?

01:02:10.310 --> 01:02:11.353
What's going on?

01:02:11.436 --> 01:02:12.938
You didn't see my text?

01:02:13.021 --> 01:02:15.732
I'm on my way
to your great-aunt's restaurant.

01:02:15.815 --> 01:02:17.901
What? Why are you going there?

01:02:17.984 --> 01:02:20.654
-[quirky music playing]
-Our next season's theme is retro.

01:02:20.737 --> 01:02:23.782
And last time I saw it, her restaurant
looked like the perfect fit.

01:02:23.865 --> 01:02:25.533
You can't go there!

01:02:25.617 --> 01:02:27.494
She hates her restaurant
getting loud and busy.

01:02:27.577 --> 01:02:29.079
She really hates it.

01:02:29.162 --> 01:02:31.414
We're not like a foodie program, though.

01:02:31.498 --> 01:02:33.667
If things go well,
we might even partner with her…

01:02:33.750 --> 01:02:36.586
No, please don't.
She might throw salt at you.

01:02:36.670 --> 01:02:39.714
She literally throws salt
when a stranger visits her.

01:02:39.798 --> 01:02:43.218
What? Do you think she'd still do that
when I'm your friend?

01:02:43.760 --> 01:02:45.178
It's okay. I'll try talking to her.

01:02:45.262 --> 01:02:49.432
Hold on.
I'll ask her about this later, so--

01:02:49.516 --> 01:02:50.850
[Ji-yun] I'm already on my way.

01:02:50.934 --> 01:02:52.394
What?

01:02:52.477 --> 01:02:54.020
I'm getting an incoming call.

01:02:54.104 --> 01:02:55.563
-Wait, Ji-yun.
-I'll call you later.

01:02:55.647 --> 01:02:57.315
Hello? Ji-yun! Hey!

01:02:57.399 --> 01:02:59.192
What? Oh no!

01:02:59.276 --> 01:03:00.318
Taxi!

01:03:00.402 --> 01:03:02.404
[quirky music continues]

01:03:08.243 --> 01:03:09.452
There's traffic.

01:03:09.536 --> 01:03:11.371
[music concludes]

01:03:12.163 --> 01:03:13.748
[pot clanging]

01:03:19.671 --> 01:03:21.131
I ACCIDENTALLY TOOK THE RESTROOM KEY

01:03:21.214 --> 01:03:23.091
I LEFT IT AT THE CONVENIENCE STORE
I'M VERY SORRY

01:03:31.808 --> 01:03:33.560
[birds chirping]

01:03:35.854 --> 01:03:37.272
[running footsteps]

01:03:37.355 --> 01:03:39.441
[panting]

01:03:39.524 --> 01:03:40.942
Ok-hui!

01:03:41.026 --> 01:03:43.778
Mi-ji must take after you.

01:03:43.862 --> 01:03:45.113
Why do you walk so fast?

01:03:45.238 --> 01:03:47.866
What is it? I need to hurry up and go.

01:03:47.949 --> 01:03:50.660
-What?
-Your mother eats porridge, right?

01:03:50.744 --> 01:03:52.162
I made abalone rice porridge.

01:03:52.245 --> 01:03:54.914
There should be enough
for you and Mi-ji too.

01:03:54.998 --> 01:03:56.374
Hey!

01:03:56.458 --> 01:03:59.544
I don't need it.
Go give it to your mother.

01:03:59.627 --> 01:04:02.213
Hey, my mother passed away.

01:04:02.964 --> 01:04:05.800
I said those things
because I have my own regrets.

01:04:05.884 --> 01:04:08.219
I couldn't be there for her final moments.

01:04:09.804 --> 01:04:11.598
[tender music playing]

01:04:11.681 --> 01:04:13.183
Hey…

01:04:13.266 --> 01:04:15.185
You know, I…

01:04:15.268 --> 01:04:16.394
You didn't know.

01:04:17.062 --> 01:04:19.689
I said things without knowing
your situation either, so we're even.

01:04:19.773 --> 01:04:20.982
Oh…

01:04:23.276 --> 01:04:25.028
You brat…

01:04:25.862 --> 01:04:29.324
How did I not know
that your mother had passed away

01:04:29.407 --> 01:04:32.160
when we've been neighbors
for ten years?

01:04:32.285 --> 01:04:35.163
I know, right? We never speak
about things like that.

01:04:35.830 --> 01:04:39.209
You should've told me
that something like that had happened.

01:04:39.292 --> 01:04:41.419
You always make me feel like the bad guy.

01:04:41.503 --> 01:04:45.048
Jeez, just take this.
We always fight if we talk for too long.

01:04:45.131 --> 01:04:47.133
You took that, so we're even.

01:04:48.218 --> 01:04:49.552
[Ok-hui] Hey!

01:04:52.347 --> 01:04:53.765
[exhales]

01:05:03.441 --> 01:05:04.651
Oh dear.

01:05:04.734 --> 01:05:06.319
[music fades]

01:05:06.403 --> 01:05:07.904
[Mi-rae exhales]

01:05:07.987 --> 01:05:09.697
-[door sliding open]
-[gasps]

01:05:09.781 --> 01:05:11.741
What took you so long?

01:05:11.825 --> 01:05:13.701
I told you
that I need to go before dinner.

01:05:13.785 --> 01:05:15.620
Okay, I got it.

01:05:15.703 --> 01:05:17.956
Since when are you so punctual?

01:05:18.039 --> 01:05:20.667
You're already late, so eat some
abalone rice porridge before you go.

01:05:20.750 --> 01:05:23.294
I told you that I'm late.
Grandma, I'll see you later.

01:05:23.378 --> 01:05:25.713
Hey, Mi-ji! Eat this before you go!

01:05:30.135 --> 01:05:31.469
What's up with her?

01:05:32.512 --> 01:05:33.680
Jeez.

01:05:36.307 --> 01:05:38.435
Isn't she acting a bit strange these days?

01:05:40.603 --> 01:05:43.440
[energetic music playing]

01:05:43.523 --> 01:05:45.150
Oh no!

01:05:45.233 --> 01:05:47.193
I'll just get out here, sir.

01:05:53.616 --> 01:05:54.993
[gasps] Damn it!

01:05:57.036 --> 01:05:59.038
[pants] Damn it!

01:06:00.665 --> 01:06:02.333
Ji-yun!

01:06:02.417 --> 01:06:04.043
[pants]

01:06:04.127 --> 01:06:05.670
I can't believe this!

01:06:05.753 --> 01:06:06.796
[car honks]

01:06:09.966 --> 01:06:11.176
[music builds]

01:06:11.259 --> 01:06:12.177
What in the world?

01:06:12.260 --> 01:06:14.512
-[panting] Wait! Stop!
-[music calms]

01:06:14.596 --> 01:06:17.098
Wait a second.
You and I should go over there…

01:06:17.182 --> 01:06:19.601
What are you doing here?
Weren't you working?

01:06:19.684 --> 01:06:22.020
Hold on. I… [panting]

01:06:22.103 --> 01:06:24.355
Wait. First…

01:06:25.315 --> 01:06:26.858
Talk with me first.

01:06:26.941 --> 01:06:29.277
-Okay, let's go in first and then--
-No!

01:06:29.360 --> 01:06:31.112
Let's go over there

01:06:31.196 --> 01:06:33.364
-and talk first…
-What's wrong with you?

01:06:33.448 --> 01:06:35.366
What are you two doing
in front of my restaurant?

01:06:35.450 --> 01:06:36.367
[music concludes]

01:06:36.451 --> 01:06:39.037
-Are you the owner, ma'am?
-Ji-yun.

01:06:39.120 --> 01:06:41.289
-I am.
-Hello, ma'am.

01:06:41.372 --> 01:06:43.458
I've been wanting to meet you for a while.

01:06:43.541 --> 01:06:47.921
Mi-rae told me that you're her great-aunt,
so I came here to meet you. I apologize.

01:06:48.004 --> 01:06:51.674
My name is Park Ji-yun.
I'm a friend of Mi-rae.

01:07:00.391 --> 01:07:06.022
I guess I should've contacted you
before coming here.

01:07:06.105 --> 01:07:10.151
Mi-rae told me that her great-aunt
doesn't like unexpected visitors.

01:07:10.235 --> 01:07:12.570
But I wanted to talk to you in person.

01:07:15.281 --> 01:07:16.824
She said that?

01:07:17.867 --> 01:07:23.039
That her great-aunt doesn't like
people just dropping by?

01:07:25.667 --> 01:07:28.002
[Mi-ji breathes deeply]

01:07:29.045 --> 01:07:32.340
[soft pensive music playing]

01:07:37.053 --> 01:07:39.764
-[woman 1 sobbing]
-[man 1] Where did you hide the money?

01:07:39.847 --> 01:07:41.599
[man 2] Where's the money? Where is it?

01:07:41.683 --> 01:07:44.060
[man 3] You take responsibility
and put that money back, okay?

01:07:44.143 --> 01:07:46.729
If you can't, call the police right now.

01:07:46.813 --> 01:07:48.481
What do you think you're doing?

01:07:48.565 --> 01:07:49.816
Who are you?

01:07:49.899 --> 01:07:51.025
Get up.

01:07:51.818 --> 01:07:53.111
[man 2] What the hell?

01:07:53.194 --> 01:07:55.071
I'm sorry I came too late.

01:07:55.154 --> 01:07:56.823
[breathing shakily]

01:07:58.908 --> 01:08:00.159
[woman 2] It's okay.

01:08:03.788 --> 01:08:06.207
[breathes deeply]

01:08:15.633 --> 01:08:17.218
You're right about one thing…

01:08:18.511 --> 01:08:20.054
and wrong about another.

01:08:23.474 --> 01:08:25.893
I am her great-aunt.

01:08:27.186 --> 01:08:29.105
But I don't hate people dropping by.

01:08:29.188 --> 01:08:30.106
[tender music playing]

01:08:30.189 --> 01:08:34.068
Since you're my great-niece's friend,
come back another time.

01:08:34.152 --> 01:08:35.361
[Ji-yun] Really?

01:08:36.195 --> 01:08:37.530
Thank you.

01:08:38.448 --> 01:08:40.241
[door bell chimes]

01:08:40.325 --> 01:08:43.328
[breathes shakily]

01:08:45.455 --> 01:08:47.165
[tender music continues]

01:09:03.681 --> 01:09:04.849
Ma'am…

01:09:07.226 --> 01:09:09.354
Why did you do that?

01:09:10.647 --> 01:09:12.565
Shouldn't I be asking you that?

01:09:18.071 --> 01:09:19.364
I'm sorry.

01:09:20.114 --> 01:09:22.158
I didn't mean to lie--

01:09:22.241 --> 01:09:23.409
[Ro-sa] It's fine.

01:09:24.494 --> 01:09:26.788
I lied for my sake too.

01:09:28.665 --> 01:09:31.042
Whenever a lie comes to light,

01:09:31.584 --> 01:09:33.419
everyone feels awful,

01:09:34.420 --> 01:09:36.422
regardless of whose lie it is.

01:09:39.384 --> 01:09:42.053
Just think of it as payment
for that cleaning you did.

01:09:49.852 --> 01:09:52.939
I doubt that you came here
to introduce your friend to me.

01:09:53.022 --> 01:09:55.358
What did your company
tell you to do this time?

01:09:55.441 --> 01:09:56.526
[music fades]

01:09:56.609 --> 01:09:57.652
Well…

01:09:58.820 --> 01:10:00.655
They told me to ask you something.

01:10:01.447 --> 01:10:03.741
But I really had no intention
of coming back here.

01:10:03.825 --> 01:10:08.329
I was just going to kill some time outside
and then go, but my friend--

01:10:08.413 --> 01:10:09.455
So?

01:10:10.540 --> 01:10:12.166
What did they want you to ask?

01:10:13.710 --> 01:10:16.963
The company wants to meet with you,

01:10:17.046 --> 01:10:20.258
so they told me to ask you
when you're available.

01:10:22.093 --> 01:10:25.012
I'll make sure to tell them
that you refused,

01:10:25.096 --> 01:10:26.681
so don't worry about it--

01:10:26.764 --> 01:10:28.725
Tell them next Friday afternoon.

01:10:28.850 --> 01:10:30.393
[soft uplifting music playing]

01:10:30.935 --> 01:10:31.811
Pardon?

01:10:31.894 --> 01:10:34.147
I say that I hate the company
for hiding behind a kid

01:10:34.230 --> 01:10:36.774
when I feel like I'm doing the same thing.

01:10:36.858 --> 01:10:39.402
If I turned you away,
what good would that do?

01:10:39.485 --> 01:10:42.029
It's better that
I tell the company myself.

01:10:42.113 --> 01:10:43.364
Ma'am.

01:10:44.407 --> 01:10:47.785
I'm not going there to sell my land.
I'm going to lodge a complaint.

01:10:47.869 --> 01:10:49.996
That's more than enough for me.

01:10:50.079 --> 01:10:53.040
Thank you so much. Thank you, ma'am.

01:10:53.124 --> 01:10:54.417
[breathes deeply]

01:10:56.210 --> 01:11:00.214
Why? She refused to open up
when I was trying to get on her good side,

01:11:00.298 --> 01:11:03.050
so why has she opened up now?

01:11:03.134 --> 01:11:04.719
[Ro-sa] Why are you just standing there?

01:11:04.802 --> 01:11:06.721
Hurry up and put the restroom key back.

01:11:07.680 --> 01:11:09.098
The restroom key?

01:11:09.182 --> 01:11:10.600
-I…
-[music concludes]

01:11:11.142 --> 01:11:14.061
I put a note on your door.
You didn't see it?

01:11:15.605 --> 01:11:16.606
A note?

01:11:17.398 --> 01:11:18.399
What note?

01:11:18.483 --> 01:11:21.944
I wrote that I left it
at the convenience store…

01:11:22.028 --> 01:11:24.530
[gasps] I'll go get it right away.

01:11:29.494 --> 01:11:30.620
[door closes]

01:11:35.041 --> 01:11:37.418
[pants]

01:11:39.587 --> 01:11:42.465
[continues panting]

01:11:45.176 --> 01:11:46.427
[groans]

01:11:50.097 --> 01:11:51.891
-[exhales heavily]
-[lights clicking on]

01:11:51.974 --> 01:11:53.017
[Mi-rae] Huh?

01:11:53.559 --> 01:11:55.770
-[crickets chirping]
-[footsteps approaching]

01:11:56.395 --> 01:11:57.688
[door opens]

01:11:58.397 --> 01:12:00.858
[Se-jin] You came just in time for dinner.

01:12:02.276 --> 01:12:03.736
You haven't eaten yet, right?

01:12:04.278 --> 01:12:05.863
I…

01:12:06.739 --> 01:12:07.949
I ate.

01:12:09.992 --> 01:12:12.537
So you were late because you were eating.

01:12:12.620 --> 01:12:15.498
It's okay. I get it.

01:12:18.167 --> 01:12:21.629
[Mi-rae] You should go eat.
I'll tidy up here.

01:12:21.712 --> 01:12:22.964
You know…

01:12:26.759 --> 01:12:27.927
About that chair…

01:12:31.347 --> 01:12:33.140
It belonged to my late grandfather.

01:12:34.183 --> 01:12:36.060
[gentle music playing]

01:12:36.143 --> 01:12:40.022
Even after I bought him an expensive one,
he kept patching up the old one

01:12:40.523 --> 01:12:42.483
and he'd only rest in that chair.

01:12:43.109 --> 01:12:45.987
I had no idea, so last time…

01:12:46.070 --> 01:12:48.364
I didn't know either until it was gone.

01:12:49.615 --> 01:12:52.243
The chair, the manual truck…

01:12:54.245 --> 01:12:56.163
Even this godforsaken strawberry farm…

01:12:57.123 --> 01:12:59.876
When my grandfather was alive,
I insisted that he throw it all away.

01:12:59.959 --> 01:13:02.378
But I regret that now,
and I can't throw it away.

01:13:03.296 --> 01:13:04.547
I tend to do that.

01:13:05.381 --> 01:13:08.926
I'm the type to make hasty judgments,
only to regret them later.

01:13:10.928 --> 01:13:11.971
So…

01:13:13.306 --> 01:13:15.725
I'm sorry for what I said
so thoughtlessly last time.

01:13:15.808 --> 01:13:16.851
Oh…

01:13:20.104 --> 01:13:22.440
And thank you for coming back.

01:13:24.275 --> 01:13:26.611
If I hadn't said this to you,
I'd have regretted it.

01:13:26.694 --> 01:13:30.448
[inhales]
I was going to tell you this last time.

01:13:30.531 --> 01:13:33.868
I just didn't know where to begin…

01:13:50.718 --> 01:13:52.345
I haven't eaten yet.

01:13:54.263 --> 01:13:55.681
What a coincidence!

01:13:56.265 --> 01:13:58.476
I made enough for two people by accident.

01:14:00.728 --> 01:14:01.854
[door opens]

01:14:02.688 --> 01:14:05.650
[Mi-rae] When people see me
as weak, pathetic, and clumsy,

01:14:05.733 --> 01:14:09.362
they usually get disappointed
and turn away from me.

01:14:10.404 --> 01:14:11.656
So why doesn't he?

01:14:11.739 --> 01:14:13.783
-[music fades]
-[door sliding open]

01:14:14.909 --> 01:14:16.577
What took you so long?

01:14:22.041 --> 01:14:23.709
I don't serve solo diners.

01:14:24.669 --> 01:14:25.878
I'm sorry.

01:14:26.712 --> 01:14:27.755
I…

01:14:29.090 --> 01:14:30.800
I should've introduced myself.

01:14:35.930 --> 01:14:38.349
[sighs] I'm late.

01:14:43.479 --> 01:14:46.565
-I'm sorry that this is all I have.
-My goodness. Thank you.

01:14:46.649 --> 01:14:50.069
Ma'am, this isn't much, but…

01:14:50.152 --> 01:14:52.571
My goodness. You didn't have to.

01:14:52.655 --> 01:14:54.615
-[soft music playing]
-I'm just happy that you came.

01:14:54.699 --> 01:14:57.702
I can't accept this.
By the way, have you eaten dinner?

01:14:57.785 --> 01:14:58.911
It's okay.

01:14:58.995 --> 01:15:00.913
No, I'll cook something
for you right away.

01:15:00.997 --> 01:15:03.708
-Just wait a little, okay? My gosh.
-[Ho-su] Yes, ma'am.

01:15:10.965 --> 01:15:13.426
I've never seen that side of her.

01:15:16.387 --> 01:15:19.598
I guess in life,
there are just moments like this.

01:15:21.100 --> 01:15:25.229
Moments where doors to people's hearts
just open without reason.

01:15:25.312 --> 01:15:26.230
[door slides open]

01:15:28.315 --> 01:15:29.650
-[Ro-sa sighs]
-[music fades]

01:15:29.734 --> 01:15:31.277
What are you doing here?

01:15:32.862 --> 01:15:34.989
Did you cut a new set of keys
or something?

01:15:37.241 --> 01:15:38.367
[door closing]

01:15:40.036 --> 01:15:42.538
Just wait a little.
I'll go make a single serving right away.

01:15:42.621 --> 01:15:43.664
[Ho-su] Yes, ma'am.

01:15:45.833 --> 01:15:47.126
A single serving.

01:15:54.175 --> 01:15:57.803
What are you doing here?
I thought you said you'd never come.

01:15:57.887 --> 01:16:00.222
You were going on
about a conflict of interest.

01:16:01.182 --> 01:16:03.017
There's no conflict of interest now.

01:16:04.852 --> 01:16:06.020
I quit my job.

01:16:07.188 --> 01:16:08.147
What?

01:16:08.230 --> 01:16:10.941
I can do anything I want now.

01:16:12.610 --> 01:16:14.278
That's why I'm going to help you.

01:16:16.489 --> 01:16:18.115
I'll help you.

01:16:21.160 --> 01:16:26.415
-[gentle pop song playing]
-[singing in Korean]

01:16:28.209 --> 01:16:33.214
[singing in Korean continues]

01:16:35.466 --> 01:16:40.679
[singing in Korean continues]

01:16:42.431 --> 01:16:47.103
[singing in Korean continues]

01:16:49.855 --> 01:16:56.612
[singing in Korean continues]

01:16:57.321 --> 01:17:01.659
[singing in Korean continues]

01:17:01.742 --> 01:17:02.785
[gate opens]

01:17:03.577 --> 01:17:06.455
[singing in Korean continues]

01:17:06.539 --> 01:17:09.291
[gate opens, closes]

01:17:11.001 --> 01:17:17.383
[singing in Korean continues]

01:17:19.385 --> 01:17:20.427
[Mi-ji] Hm?

01:17:20.511 --> 01:17:25.432
[singing in Korean continues]

01:17:25.516 --> 01:17:30.396
[singing in Korean continues]

01:17:30.479 --> 01:17:33.023
[Mi-ji] You take longer
and longer every day.

01:17:33.107 --> 01:17:34.608
I waited ages for you.

01:17:34.692 --> 01:17:37.444
[singing in Korean continues]

01:17:39.363 --> 01:17:44.618
[singing in Korean continues]

01:17:46.036 --> 01:17:47.621
[puppies barking]

01:17:47.705 --> 01:17:51.125
[singing in Korean continues]

01:17:52.042 --> 01:17:53.502
[giggles]

01:17:54.795 --> 01:18:00.050
[singing in Korean continues]

01:18:00.134 --> 01:18:01.302
YU MI-JI

01:18:01.385 --> 01:18:03.179
[Mi-ji] Why do you seem so down now?

01:18:03.262 --> 01:18:06.594
I think the firm I quit
was the best I could ever achieve.

01:18:06.694 --> 01:18:09.319
[Mi-ji] That won't do. Let's go.
There has to be something you enjoy.

01:18:09.400 --> 01:18:11.194
[Ho-su] Why are you being so nice to me?

01:18:11.270 --> 01:18:13.981
[nurse] Have you had a chance
to check this month's payment?

01:18:14.139 --> 01:18:16.150
[Ok-hui]
Is something going on with Mi-rae?

01:18:16.259 --> 01:18:17.934
Is it okay to use Mi-rae's money, then?

01:18:18.043 --> 01:18:19.878
So work comes before Grandma now?

01:18:19.973 --> 01:18:21.373
Is it as easy as you thought?

01:18:21.447 --> 01:18:23.699
[Ho-su] Is the reunion you mentioned
this weekend?

01:18:23.782 --> 01:18:25.326
[Ji-yun] I didn't tell her on purpose.

01:18:25.409 --> 01:18:28.495
[Mi-ji] I'll be there too. If I don't go,
they'll say whatever they want.

01:18:28.579 --> 01:18:30.164
"Mi-rae this" and "Mi-rae that."

01:18:30.247 --> 01:18:31.123
See you there.

01:18:37.621 --> 01:18:39.623
Subtitle translation by Jane Jung
